{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate","id":365654,"title":"Kilomote and the Loom of Fate?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-10T12:58:49-08:00","id":365654,"title":"Kilomote and the Loom of Fate?","content":"It's been a while since a subject like this came up, but if a Kilomote gets used somewhere in some Sorcery Spell, what shows up on the Loom? Do the Sidereals know what's happening specifically, or do they just know some Solar is doing something in that general vicinity of Creation? How likely is the Bronze Faction and the Wyld Hunt to respond?<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry for the spelling errors. I am away on my iPhone right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 01-10-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T13:46:10-08:00","id":365719,"title":"","content":"Might help to mention what a Kilomeye is is or at least where to find it. Because I've never heard of this thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:30:26-08:00","id":365748,"title":"","content":"Since the only entities with access to a pool of 1,000 motes are Primordials, I would think they'd have bigger problems than a single spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:55:07-08:00","id":365758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365748#post365748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the only entities with access to a pool of 1,000 motes are Primordials, I would think they'd have bigger problems than a single spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordials AND (Unity of the Closed Fist + Advanced Essence capacitors) <br /> <br /> Granted you would need some heavy duty Spirits to work with you.<br /> <br /> Also, Kilomote = 1000 motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T15:09:24-08:00","id":365789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365719#post365719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might help to mention what a Kilomeye is is or at least where to find it. Because I've never heard of this thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it's a &quot;kilo<i>mote</i>,&quot; as in a concentration of 1000 motes of Essence into a condensed location or entity. I've heard it mentioned before in reference to things that consume vast amounts of Essence, like First Age experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Burn Legend -- Advent of Yomi Wan <a href=\"http://burnlegend.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://burnlegend.blogspot.com/</a><br /> EX3 -- Dawn of Resurgent Sun <a href=\"https://resurgentsun.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://resurgentsun.wordpress.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3140-greyeyes","name":"GreyEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T15:15:40-08:00","id":365792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreyEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365789#post365789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe it's a &amp;quot;kilo<i>mote</i>,&amp;quot; as in a concentration of 1000 motes of Essence into a condensed location or entity. I've heard it mentioned before in reference to things that consume vast amounts of Essence, like First Age experiments.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was actually one of the first things that got the Sidereals worried about the Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T15:50:30-08:00","id":365817,"title":"","content":"Good lord you have a habit of latching on to the most terrible parts of the setting and running with them.<br /> <br /> My vote is that it does nothing special other than waste a thousand motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:08:54-08:00","id":365841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365817#post365817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good lord you have a habit of latching on to the most terrible parts of the setting and running with them.<br /> <br /> My vote is that it does nothing special other than waste a thousand motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that you and another researcher observe some minor teleportation effect when no one else is looking. You and your colleague try to convince people of it, but are laughed out of academics and languish in obscurity, only to be vindicated a century later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:15:53-08:00","id":365847,"title":"","content":"I'll need to do some research. There aren't many references to kilomotes in Exalted to use as a baseline. That said I think the Five-metal Shriek can store a Kilomote of energy and Sids don't track it or even know where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T17:59:42-08:00","id":365885,"title":"","content":"I highly doubt kilomotes are still a thing. Of all the ways to represent vast unfathomable power in the setting, &quot;1000 motes&quot; is about as boring as it can get; and the whole conceit behind them was based on Yozis using Infernal Exalted charms (intended for PCs) and therefore needing something else on top of them.<br /> <br /> The Yozis in 3e probably don't have kilomotes because they probably don't have mechanics for mote pools or anything of that nature. Other people don't have kilomotes because (once you get past the initial &quot;wow, a <i>thousand</i>&quot; awe) you realize that they don't really accomplish anything mechanically you would actually want -- do you intend for whoever is wielding the kilomote to ever run out of motes? If so (assuming you haven't given them equally outrageous charm costs, which defeats the purpose), why are you making it such a boring protracted process? If not, why give them any mote pool at all rather than throttling their powers in other ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-10-2015, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T18:09:32-08:00","id":365888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365758#post365758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordials AND (Unity of the Closed Fist + Advanced Essence capacitors)</div> </div> </div> </div>So Primordials/cheesy bullshit/magitech of questionably-appropriate thematics, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T18:20:02-08:00","id":365893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365847#post365847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need to do some research. There aren't many references to kilomotes in Exalted to use as a baseline. That said I think the Five-metal Shriek can store a Kilomote of energy and Sids don't track it or even know where it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check Manses explosions, I forget if it is essence build up or Thousand Forged Dragons, and the discharges in the Pole of Lightning. Both of those use the term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T18:49:41-08:00","id":365905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365817#post365817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good lord you have a habit of latching on to the most terrible parts of the setting and running with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just imagining my Solaroid looking up his last incarnation's mentor/best friend who betrayed him during the Usurpation and finding out when he is scheduled to oversee the Loom of Fate. The Sidereal, who is an old man now, is sitting down munching on a biscuit while staring at the weave of destiny and then BOO! he shits a brick and develops an ulcer. <br /> <br /> Actually, don't some spells rely on Craft Fate? I'll bet I could make that an Adamant circle spell for people who are watching the Loom of Fate. Something to do in between playing Grand Theft Yeddim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 01-11-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:02:54-08:00","id":365935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365885#post365885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highly doubt kilomotes are still a thing. Of all the ways to represent vast unfathomable power in the setting, &amp;quot;1000 motes&amp;quot; is about as boring as it can get; and the whole conceit behind them was based on Yozis using Infernal Exalted charms (intended for PCs) and therefore needing something else on top of them.<br /> <br /> The Yozis in 3e probably don't have kilomotes because they probably don't have mechanics for mote pools or anything of that nature. Other people don't have kilomotes because (once you get past the initial &amp;quot;wow, a <i>thousand</i>&amp;quot; awe) you realize that they don't really accomplish anything mechanically you would actually want -- do you intend for whoever is wielding the kilomote to ever run out of motes? If so (assuming you haven't given them equally outrageous charm costs, which defeats the purpose), why are you making it such a boring protracted process? If not, why give them any mote pool at all rather than throttling their powers in other ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thousand mote pool is simply a way of showing that even the Yozis can run out of juice at some point but it's really hard for them. It's okay for an Exalted to burn out at some point, but the Yozis are supposed to be able to hang in there unless you have their kryptonite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:35:08-08:00","id":365992,"title":"","content":"Okay. I'm seeing a number of questions along these lines, and I understand. The book says things like 'Essence use disturbs destiny' and all that, so it's pretty easy to make assumptions along the lines of 'The raw power radiating out damages the giant fate machine!'<br /> <br /> What you have to understand is that 'What happens if 1000 motes' isn't an interesting question because the volume of essence is only tangentially related to the Loom. The Loom of Fate has descriptive and predictive functions, and it's totally capable of tracking enormously powerful things. Greater Elemental Dragons, mountain-sized monsters, entire cities of sorcerers- those aren't automatically disruptions in the lines of destiny. <br /> <br /> What disrupts the Loom of Fate is when a things happen which had basically no chance of happening. If your Solar casts Rain of Doom and melts a city to nothing, that came out of nowhere. The disruption is equal exactly to the Loom being wrong about everything in that area suddenly melting in a torrent of acid. Using the proper magic, or planning, you can mitigate that entirely by letting Heaven know that someone is going to melt everything with acid rains.<br /> <br /> If you use those thousand motes to temporarily look really cool, then you'll get virtually no discernible disruption at all. If you use the thousand motes to transform an entire nation into a pillar of fire which spews out fire-birds to fly around and drop fire-shit on people, it will be a massive disruption (although not something the Loom hasn't seen before). If you use it to create a creation-spanning megaplague which kills 100% of everyone, you essentially break the Loom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:41:19-08:00","id":366000,"title":"","content":"The big thing to consider is that we basically have no rules whatsoever for Fate Error. It is strongly suggested that they can cause by massive expenditures of Essence. What shows up in the Loom would be highly dependent on what the Kilomote is used to accomplish.<br /> <br /> The Thousand-Forged Dragon can absorb energy from a Manse and the surrounding area to release a multi-kilomote explosion. The effect being 100 dice of damage in a (manse rating) miles area. The results should show up in the Loom as the threads of everything in the blast radius being cut short. The destruction of the demesne and mangled dragon lines should also show up prominently.<br /> <br /> The Five-Metal Shrike on the otherhand only uses a half-kilomote and does infinite damage in a 25 yard radius and 50 levels of damage in a 500 yard radius. Less energy, smaller radius, but really far more damaging. Again death and destruction on a truely massive scale.<br /> <br /> For comparison the Adamant Sorcery Spell Total Annihilation only costs 65 motes. This spell does 50 Levels of damage in a 50 yard radius and expands for Essencex5 ticks at a rate of 10 yards/tick doing 25 Levels of damage/action. <br /> <br /> The most notable thing here is the obvious loss of efficiency as mote expenditure goes up. A Kilomote might be pretty, but I doubt it will show up on the Loom in an appreciably greater way than the Total Annihilation spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:50:22-08:00","id":366003,"title":"","content":"I just got a new plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:34:40-08:00","id":366024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365992#post365992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I'm seeing a number of questions along these lines, and I understand. The book says things like 'Essence use disturbs destiny' and all that, so it's pretty easy to make assumptions along the lines of 'The raw power radiating out damages the giant fate machine!'</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a line somewhere about essence expenditure causing the threads of fate to vibrate. If the Threads vibrate enough they can stick to and tangle with other threads. This being how you get strange fate errors where the destiny of an empire lays in the fate of a toad half-way across Creation. I didn't bring it up because the only known uses for a kilomote would result in most all relevant threads being cut from the loom by their deaths, and the Exalted aren't burdened by the pull of destiny.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:40:23-08:00","id":366026,"title":"","content":"I think their main priority would be, where did all this energy come from and where did it all go. Best case is someone just detonated a first age bomb, worst case they just used a very potent ritual or artifact. Directly it would probably give the pattern spiders something to do but sidereals would have bigger concerns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:50:04-08:00","id":366043,"title":"","content":"The Loom of Fate has a kill-switch protocol that isolates and extracts moments in which the phrase &quot;kilomote&quot; is used from reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T22:09:07-08:00","id":366055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366043#post366043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loom of Fate has a kill-switch protocol that isolates and extracts moments in which the phrase &quot;kilomote&quot; is used from reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I wanted to make my next Twilight a Professor of Kilomotonic Studies.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know, my research has revealed something we could use to resolve just this problem--&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you going to suggest throwing a thousand motes at it again?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then I fail to get tenure at the university because they discover that I actually used a thousand <i>and one</i> motes for some of my most famous feats, bringing shame to the entire field of kilomotonic studies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-11-2015, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T23:00:55-08:00","id":366084,"title":"","content":"&quot;Chejop... I... sir, I have terrible news. We have discovered that the Solars have constructed the <i>Giga</i>mote!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I was afraid this day might come. Initiate Order 66 immediately.&quot;<br /> <br /> - conversation that occurred shortly before the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T03:55:57-08:00","id":366190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365817#post365817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good lord you have a habit of latching on to the most terrible parts of the setting and running with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit personal and rather hostile, can we be careful about those things in future please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T06:06:34-08:00","id":366224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366190#post366190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a bit personal and rather hostile, can we be careful about those things in future please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. The pattern had been building for a while and then I saw &quot;kilomote&quot; and then red. I'll stay out of these threads from now on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T06:19:06-08:00","id":366229,"title":"","content":"Roughly how much is a mote in Joules, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T09:01:13-08:00","id":366353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366229#post366229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roughly how much is a mote in Joules, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e painted it as a lot. As in, all of the power of a Solar was equivalent to lots of nuclear bombs, at least in raw form. 2e always did like to go overboard on the shonen fighting aesthetic, though. It's on page 179, and it went super overboard when it used the nukes actually used in wartime on people as a reference point for how much power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T09:03:47-08:00","id":366358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366224#post366224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. The pattern had been building for a while and then I saw &amp;quot;kilomote&amp;quot; and then red. I'll stay out of these threads from now on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally found your criticism constructive, and for what it's worth I will watch myself in the future. Also, my apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T09:22:43-08:00","id":366376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365992#post365992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I'm seeing a number of questions along these lines, and I understand. The book says things like 'Essence use disturbs destiny' and all that, so it's pretty easy to make assumptions along the lines of 'The raw power radiating out damages the giant fate machine!'<br /> <br /> What you have to understand is that 'What happens if 1000 motes' isn't an interesting question because the volume of essence is only tangentially related to the Loom. The Loom of Fate has descriptive and predictive functions, and it's totally capable of tracking enormously powerful things. Greater Elemental Dragons, mountain-sized monsters, entire cities of sorcerers- those aren't automatically disruptions in the lines of destiny.<br /> <br /> What disrupts the Loom of Fate is when a things happen which had basically no chance of happening. If your Solar casts Rain of Doom and melts a city to nothing, that came out of nowhere. The disruption is equal exactly to the Loom being wrong about everything in that area suddenly melting in a torrent of acid. Using the proper magic, or planning, you can mitigate that entirely by letting Heaven know that someone is going to melt everything with acid rains.<br /> <br /> If you use those thousand motes to temporarily look really cool, then you'll get virtually no discernible disruption at all. If you use the thousand motes to transform an entire nation into a pillar of fire which spews out fire-birds to fly around and drop fire-shit on people, it will be a massive disruption (although not something the Loom hasn't seen before). If you use it to create a creation-spanning megaplague which kills 100% of everyone, you essentially break the Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was reading through the Sidereals book and found the &quot;high essence expenditures mess up the loom&quot; to be pretty stupid and confusing. Looking at it as a &quot;high mote expenditures are often correlated with highly implausible/unexpected happenings&quot; makes the paragraphs about the loom make much more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T11:59:34-08:00","id":366515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366229#post366229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roughly how much is a mote in Joules, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence can't be measured as an energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T12:12:41-08:00","id":366537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366229#post366229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roughly how much is a mote in Joules, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence most likely the essential nature of what a thing is. The basic unit being the Mote which likely equates to basically being the Essence of existing. What can happen is the Essence is transformed, into the Essence of Energy allowing it to become or produce Energy in its purest form.<br /> <br /> Basically, Energy isn't a property of Essence, but rather Essence is a property of Energy as it is of all things,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:40:40-08:00","id":366720,"title":"","content":"As much as I'd like to someday do an in-joke about X being over 9 kilomotes, I'm happy to see the whole idea dying off with the other wacky pseudo-sci-fi setting aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T18:13:35-08:00","id":366783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366515#post366515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence can't be measured as an energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the thing to consider is that essence and motes don't need to be a scientific measurement or unit on which Creation operates, the only reason they need to have a numerical value applied to them is that they are one of the resourced based balances of the game not the world (along with resources things like willpower and health). A Dawn doesn't think &quot;I only have 10 motes left that means I can Iron Whirlwind once and apply Hungry Tiger to each attack&quot;, the actual though process is &quot;I'm being pushed to my limits, I need to make this attack count, it's the last chance I have&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the same token, sure there may be immense applications of power in Creation that could use a &quot;Kilomote&quot; of essence, but a Sorcerer or Primordial isn't measuring out the the exact number of motes with a Orichalcum Multimeter, they are going to approach the situation with a much more abstract view, going with the amount of essence that FEELS right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T22:15:24-08:00","id":367019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=366515#post366515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence can't be measured as an energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know that there are artifacts that require X motes, or that can store X motes. So a mote of Essence is a discrete amount, and you can probably measure how much energy you get out of 5 motes versus say, 10 motes (putting 5 motes into an artifact that requires 10 motes isn't going to be good enough). So it's probably possible to measure how much energy a single mote is capable of putting out, thus the entire field of Motonic Physics back during the First Age.<br /> <br /> But enough about that, have a joke.<br /> <br /> Q: How many Solars does it take to change a lightbulb?<br /> <br /> A: A Solar doesn't need a lightbulb when it's easier for her to just strangle the darkness to death with her bare hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T22:45:41-08:00","id":367057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367019#post367019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we know that there are artifacts that require X motes, or that can store X motes. So a mote of Essence is a discrete amount, and you can probably measure how much energy you get out of 5 motes versus say, 10 motes (putting 5 motes into an artifact that requires 10 motes isn't going to be good enough). So it's probably possible to measure how much energy a single mote is capable of putting out, thus the entire field of Motonic Physics back during the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Motonic physics&quot; is equivalent to trying to understand things like the soul, love, or religions by reducing them to a set of physics equations. Essence isn't described in the empirical and the experiential; it's intrinsically spiritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T23:02:42-08:00","id":367071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367057#post367057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Motonic physics&quot; is equivalent to trying to understand things like the soul, love, or religions by reducing them to a set of physics equations. Essence isn't described in the empirical and the experiential; it's intrinsically spiritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls are discrete things in Exalted too, and you can touch them, break them apart and dig into them, and figure out how they work. Love is also somewhat easier to understand in Creation - there's an entire bureau devoted to it in Yu-Shan where they plan out all the details. If someone has never experienced the emotion of love before, it's probably because there was a slip in the paperwork somewhere along the lines.<br /> <br /> At least in prior editions, Essence was the basic building block of Creation (in the same way that atoms are the basic building block in our universe), and I kind of liked the sense that First Age Exalted had begun to dissect it and study something that, in the 2nd Age, was viewed more as a mythical thing. It was an example of the &quot;lost knowledge&quot; of the prior age.<br /> <br /> But, I admit, I've always been kind of a fan of that sense of meta-knowledge in the game - that &quot;Essence&quot; and &quot;Motes&quot; (and souls and love) are things that actually exist in the setting, and you can deal with those as discrete entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T23:14:34-08:00","id":367077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367071#post367071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Souls are discrete things in Exalted too, and you can touch them, break them apart and dig into them, and figure out how they work. Love is also somewhat easier to understand in Creation - there's an entire bureau devoted to it in Yu-Shan where they plan out all the details. If someone has never experienced the emotion of love before, it's probably because there was a slip in the paperwork somewhere along the lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how Heaven works, even in past editions. If you jump into a river, there's no paperwork that needs to be filed so that you land in the river, or so that you are appropriately soaked/chilled. And if you kill a river god, the river doesn't just vanish: the gods are not the rivers. They're managers. The paperwork that needs to be filed (if any does) when you jump would be that mortal So-and-So jumped in the river at so-and-so time and place. Descriptive, not prescriptive.<br /> <br /> Sure, gods can meddle, but even then the paperwork is to allow them to meddle properly, with the sanction of heaven. To get results someone has to go over and an work some sort of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T23:26:09-08:00","id":367081,"title":"","content":"This isn't a &quot;God is not the River&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> Fate is important, and it can have an effect on people. If someone is fated to not fall in love, while it is <i>possible</i> that they will (because Fate can always be glitched and other gods/Exalted, etc can use their powers to change things), it's terribly unlikely. Likewise if someone is fated to fall in love with another person, then they probably will (barring some outside interference).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if none of that matters, and it's just &quot;descriptive&quot; rather than &quot;prescriptive&quot; then the entire Bureau of Fate is pointless, and that isn't much fun for Sidereal players. Why should Players be too worried about planning Fate and running around fixing things when they go wrong, if the only issue is that someone's paperwork ended up being a little off?<br /> <br /> Fate does matter, it has an effect on things, and when it gets messed up, it's important for Creation that things be put back on track, not just because it messed up some gods paperwork.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*<br /> <br /> I mean, when Prince Joe peeks out of his carriage and falls in love with the commoner walking across the street, that isn't really spiritual or a mystery or anything like that. To <i>him</i> it probably is, yes. But we, as readers, know it's something that was probably approved by a planning committee up in Yu-Shan several years ago, and only after they had weighed out the pro's and con's to determine if it's better for the future of Creation or not.<br /> <br /> And then, when all is said and done, maybe they had to send a Sidereal agent to make sure that the prince fell in love with that commoner and not the Fair Folk next to her that was trying to tempt him.<br /> <br /> Some of the things that other settings treat a mysterious, Exalted treats differently. And I have always found that to be something that makes Exalted kind of cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-12-2015, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T01:40:04-08:00","id":367135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we know that there are artifacts that require X motes, or that can store X motes. So a mote of Essence is a discrete amount, and you can probably measure how much energy you get out of 5 motes versus say, 10 motes (putting 5 motes into an artifact that requires 10 motes isn't going to be good enough). So it's probably possible to measure how much energy a single mote is capable of putting out, thus the entire field of Motonic Physics back during the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say characters still articulate motes as &quot;units&quot; of Essence when discussion of something being fueled or used up comes up, but even the name feels kind of non-specific and just a reference to dust motes. In the mechanics, mote values just seem like a way to balance and regulate the use of different Charms, since Charms with the same mote cost can logically entail different amounts of energy, especially when used by different Exalted, and they don't really seem to scale with one another in a manner that implies five motes providing five times the energy of one mote. When you've got things like fire lances, motes seem less about how much energy they provide and more about just being a kind of ammunition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:15:19-08:00","id":367165,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more along the lines of Soulfire Crystals, or Lightning Boxes or other artifacts that can store &quot;X&quot; number of motes. And you have artifacts that require &quot;X&quot; number of motes to function. So I think, even in setting, there is an understanding that Essence is a thing you can mathematically calculate, and put numbers to and &quot;stick in a pot&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is something that has often been treated as energy (&quot;Spend one mote to turn on these First Age lanterns!&quot;), and it's something that has often been measured, so it just seemed odd that Vance would say Essence is something that can't be measured as energy, so I was hoping for some clarification.<br /> <br /> I will agree though that charms are a very different beast, especially from different Exalted. Some Exalted are &quot;more efficient&quot; at using Essence than others, and some charms are more efficient than other charms, which is why you can have a similar effect cost radically different amounts of energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-12-2015, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T03:44:29-08:00","id":367186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367057#post367057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Motonic physics&quot; is equivalent to trying to understand things like the soul, love, or religions by reducing them to a set of physics equations. Essence isn't described in the empirical and the experiential; it's intrinsically spiritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never heard of Medieval Christianity have you? Because the sheer amount of ink spilled and sheep slaughtered to design equations for those subjects in that period by priests would make Carjack commit suicide from pure inadequacy. Once you deal with Two Swords Theory, you realize that there is nothing that will not be dissected by someone with too much time and a hankering for mutton. And lest we leave the rest of the world hanging, Hinduism has entire hollowed-out mountains of stuff that would put the Royal Society to shame.<br /> <br /> And I fully believe that Joe Solar has no idea what his mote pool is. But Tina Twilight can figure out motes doing some rather elementary experiments based upon the easiest Charm and how many times it can be used before she is out of juice. Hell, if a Charm boosts lifting capacity, all you need to do is measure the difference in the weight able to be lifted before and after invoking it, and a comparison of its uses vis-a-vis the earlier mote-calibration experiment would eadily create a mote-to-joule equation. And Joe Solar still has no idea about this, just as my graduate-school-educated ass has no clue as to my current calorie pool. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Lets not call out specific US states as symbols of ignorance.<br /> -PenDragon</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-12-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:02:45-08:00","id":367363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367186#post367186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you deal with Two Swords Theory, you realize that there is nothing that will not be dissected by someone with too much time and a hankering for mutton.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly...our own history proves that humans are so insatiably curious that there's nothing considered so sacred that someone won't strap it to a table and vivisect it to try and figure out how it works. <br /> <br /> I can get behind people jumping over mountains, drop kicking behemoths and using completely implausible weaponry. The idea that every single scholarly Exalt ever has looked at their own powers and abilities and said to themselves &quot;No, this is far too creepy and kooky, mysterious and spooky, all together ooky, and altogether too PROFOUND A MYSTICAL AND SPIRITUAL EXPERIENCE for me to study seriously. Guess I'll just go back to breeding heroin pissing dinosaurs and bees that sting people with friendship&quot; is beyond any sense of plausability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:07:44-08:00","id":367369,"title":"","content":"&quot;Essence can't be measured as energy? CHALLENGE FUCKING ACCEPTED.&quot; - At least one Twilight at some point, presumably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-12-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:19:49-08:00","id":367379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367186#post367186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've never heard of Medieval Christianity have you? Because the sheer amount of ink spilled and sheep slaughtered to design equations for those subjects in that period by priests would make Carjack commit suicide from pure inadequacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine, but we're in a very different world now because those people didn't succeed than we would be if they had. <br /> <br /> Likewise creation is a very different place if these are matters of open debate, discussion (and even poetry!), the kind of issues that might spur a difference of opinion between sorcerous societies and spur great sages to keep rooms where the walls are entirely covered in notes than it would be if three sages observe a feat of magic and mutter amoungst themselves 'Seventeen motes. Eighteen? No, definitely seventeen'.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:24:18-08:00","id":367381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367369#post367369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Essence can't be measure as energy? CHALLENGE FUCKING ACCEPTED.&quot; - At least one Twilight at some point, presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty easy to measure how much work is required to jump a certain distance. But is a Charm just doing work in a manner that's recognizable, or something weirder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:27:57-08:00","id":367386,"title":"","content":"^^One power reading doesn't tell you much. You'd need to take it and apply complex arcane formulas to the variable and test and experiment and ultimately it becomes the final piece of a large complex puzzle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-12-2015, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:30:00-08:00","id":367388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367381#post367381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's pretty easy to measure how much work is required to jump a certain distance. But is a Charm just doing work in a manner that's recognizable, or something weirder?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are going to assume that Charms are natural extensions of skill then we must also assume that they use natural mechanisms to achieve their results. Solar mountain jumping style is accomplished by jumping not magical levitation, happy thoughts, and pixy dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:53:02-08:00","id":367428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367186#post367186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've never heard of Medieval Christianity have you? Because the sheer amount of ink spilled and sheep slaughtered to design equations for those subjects in that period by priests would make Carjack commit suicide from pure inadequacy. Once you deal with Two Swords Theory, you realize that there is nothing that will not be dissected by someone with too much time and a hankering for mutton. And lest we leave the rest of the world hanging, Hinduism has entire hollowed-out mountains of stuff that would put the Royal Society to shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because you can try to write out a set of physics to describe something doesn't mean that produces useful results. I could know everything about the play of molecules in the brain that produces love, and it still doesn't help me get the Cute Barista to look at at me. <br /> <br /> In the same way, using the times that Essence behaves with an energy-nature and trying to mathematically describe it based on that will produce results that may be accurate, aren't likely to be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:58:57-08:00","id":367434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367388#post367388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are going to assume that Charms are natural extensions of skill</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a sensible assumption to make though? <br /> <br /> I mean, surely there's no amount of being skilled with a sword that would enable you to materialise one out of thin air (Glorious Solar Saber) or hurl bolts of pure energy off your weapon (Blazing Solar Bolt). It's clear that at least some Charms are happening by supernatural means, so if you're going to make an assumption one way or another I would have thought it would be towards pixie dust, not away from it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:00:01-08:00","id":367436,"title":"","content":"^^Well, yeah, but we're all <i>mortals.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-12-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:04:25-08:00","id":367438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367428#post367428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you can try to write out a set of physics to describe something doesn't mean that produces useful results. I could know everything about the play of molecules in the brain that produces love, and it still doesn't help me get the Cute Barista to look at at me.<br /> <br /> In the same way, using the times that Essence behaves with an energy-nature and trying to mathematically describe it based on that will produce results that may be accurate, aren't likely to be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>People say that kinda stuff about NASA too. &quot;All well and good that you there are learning all this stuff, but what is the practical value of it all? Flying to the moon ain't gonna help put food on my table! Stop wasting money on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Motonic Physics is a wonderfully fascinating topic to study, but it probably does require a degree of technological advancement that Creation does not possess to turn out much practical value. Doesn't mean that you can't empirically study it, or that it has no value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:39:08-08:00","id":367463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367438#post367438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say that kinda stuff about NASA too. &quot;All well and good that you there are learning all this stuff, but what is the practical value of it all? Flying to the moon ain't gonna help put food on my table! Stop wasting money on it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's quite a different thing to talk about the actual pursuit of knowledge, and a stylistic decision about the place (or not) of describing magic as particle physics in an RPG. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:58:09-08:00","id":367477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367438#post367438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say that kinda stuff about NASA too. &quot;All well and good that you there are learning all this stuff, but what is the practical value of it all? Flying to the moon ain't gonna help put food on my table! Stop wasting money on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Motonic Physics is a wonderfully fascinating topic to study, but it probably does require a degree of technological advancement that Creation does not possess to turn out much practical value. Doesn't mean that you can't empirically study it, or that it has no value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a good equivalency. The problem isn't that you can't &quot;apply&quot; motonic science, but that the scientific method is just not a useful way to approach Essence and gives no productive results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:07:03-08:00","id":367483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367381#post367381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty easy to measure how much work is required to jump a certain distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd be surprised how hard that is, frankly. Mechanical efficiency causes variance in the effort a single task requires even if we're dealing with some kind of jumping machine, and when you're dealing with idiosyncratic generalized athletic organisms it's enormously variable. Essence may well work the same way -- after all, if I were making a game where you had to spend resources to jump, it'd probably be very simple and quantized, but this wouldn't reflect the underlying complexity.<br /> <br /> That's closer to how I tend to tend to view it than &quot;Essence can't be understood scientifically! *theremin noises*&quot;, but you can easily pile enough X-factors on to make it <i>functionally</i> virtually impossible to measure usefully, without changing how it works on a practical level in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:34:04-08:00","id":367517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367477#post367477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a good equivalency. The problem isn't that you can't &quot;apply&quot; motonic science, but that the scientific method is just not a useful way to approach Essence and gives no productive results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see people staying things like that about the Scientific Method in relation to magic, and it strongly suggests a great misunderstanding of how the Scientific Method works. Unless your Magic, in the case Essence, arbitrarily changes rules and behaviors in response to active scrutiny the Scientific Method works perfectly for developing an understanding of it. Understanding in turn would produce some form of practical application. Even this the Scientific Method would in fact turn up results that say the rules and behavior of the subject studied change in response to active scrutiny. Given that Quantum Physics is half way there already and turning out wonders left and right I expect there would still be lots of practical application to the study of Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:03:32-08:00","id":367561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367517#post367517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see people staying things like that about the Scientific Method in relation to magic, and it strongly suggests a great misunderstanding of how the Scientific Method works. Unless your Magic, in the case Essence, arbitrarily changes rules and behaviors in response to active scrutiny the Scientific Method works perfectly for developing an understanding of it. Understanding in turn would produce some form of practical application. Even this the Scientific Method would in fact turn up results that say the rules and behavior of the subject studied change in response to active scrutiny. Given that Quantum Physics is half way there already and turning out wonders left and right I expect there would still be lots of practical application to the study of Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirituality is not gonna get thrown out and replaced with scientific rationalism in Creation. Essence is not something you can approach empirically and understand. It requires spiritual, transcendent experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:17:23-08:00","id":367568,"title":"","content":"There are many different scientific branches and research methodologies. The ones I would apply to study what is essentially mythography do not at all resemble the ones I would apply to particle physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:36:51-08:00","id":367603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367428#post367428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you can try to write out a set of physics to describe something doesn't mean that produces useful results. I could know everything about the play of molecules in the brain that produces love, and it still doesn't help me get the Cute Barista to look at at me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of ways to make the barista do more than look at you, actually. And many do not require roofies.<br /> <br /> Also, in real life, spiritual things have no reproducible, observable effects. In fact, they are totally subjective and non-confirmable - the sheer number of religious hucksters shows that. But motes perform reproducible, observable effects. Even if we predicate this on the fact that Charms are not known as a thing in Creation, it is known that certain people (the Exalted) can manipulate something to get things done that are not-normal. And they can do this again and again until such a point as they cannot until time spent in not performing stressful activities has went by. These are provable things. And if one keeps narrowing the parameters of the exercise, one can home in on knowable facts. And if one is a Solar with high intelligence, access to artifact creation, and Charms to boost your abilities, it is almost impossible not to start banging away at the problem of &quot;what is a mote&quot;, even without any preconceived notions of what a mote and a Charm are. Withotu any actual ability to succeed, humans have merrily wasted their lives trying to order the angels. When you can sit there and watch Joe Solar lift 30 tons exactly 7 times an hour, it requires one to be so clueless and uninquisitive as to be not-human to not at least try and figure out the parameters of what he's doing. &quot;it's all mysterious and unknowable&quot; means nothing when anybody can sit there with a stick and a bare patch of ground and count the iterations, much less the uber-smart chick with part of the god of perfection stuck in her spleen, who only has the deific spleen because she is both inquisitive and predisposed to do something with what she learns..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:51:06-08:00","id":367614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367019#post367019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we know that there are artifacts that require X motes, or that can store X motes. So a mote of Essence is a discrete amount, and you can probably measure how much energy you get out of 5 motes versus say, 10 motes (putting 5 motes into an artifact that requires 10 motes isn't going to be good enough). So it's probably possible to measure how much energy a single mote is capable of putting out, thus the entire field of Motonic Physics back during the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would qualify this as something that players know, but not really something that characters know, with the exception of some outlier situations. For example things get a little fuzzy when you start considering the Crafters who understand the creation of artifacts that treat essence like the charge of a battery or even simply as ammunition. I feel like these application of essence diminish it as a whole, instead of being the manifest force of heroic willpower or titanic elemental beings, essence just becomes something more base, a magical Duracell battery. I still love me some Magitech, and I have no problem with the first age being a time of industrial wonder, but I think that technology should be parsed out as something distinctly mundane (albeit technologically advanced) in comparison traditional artifacts.<br /> <br /> If you want your magitech item to be an artifact as well then by all means do so, but treat it like anything else that can be either mundane or an artifact. Craftsman can make a boat and that's all it is just a boat, but he can also make an artifact vessel capable of performing feats beyond the mundane, sailing in hurricanes unscathed. Translate this idea to a magitech item like a firelance and you could have a mundane version which runs on a battery* and spits bolts of fire (*not an essence battery, just a regular one), but you could also have a Artifact version which has no battery as it is attuned to its wielder, capable of firing gouts of flame like Hesiesh's own breath, leaving a path of roiling fireballs only dreamed of by Michael Bay in its wake.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:02:23-08:00","id":367661,"title":"","content":"Studying matter would definitely be too broad. You're talking about some sort of &quot;materials science&quot;, which is nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:22:59-08:00","id":367681,"title":"","content":"On your character sheet, cross out &quot;Essence&quot; and replace it with your character name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:29:41-08:00","id":367684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367561#post367561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirituality is not gonna get thrown out and replaced with scientific rationalism in Creation. Essence is not something you can approach empirically and understand. It requires spiritual, transcendent experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Creation obeys different rules than our own world does, doesn't mean that scientific rationalism doesn't exist - it just means that it will follow the laws of Creation.<br /> <br /> I mean, there are lots of things you can study, scientifically, about Essence. You can figure out how it changes, or how it flows, how it affects the world around it, how it can be channeled in one way to do one thing, or in another way to do something else. These are what the &quot;sciences&quot; of the Exalted world, such as Geomancy or Alchemy or Probablistics are based around. And people learned these, presumably, through experimentation rather than direct divine inspiration.<br /> <br /> In fact, Thaumaturgy, Sorcery and Charms and &quot;magic&quot; in Creation are all products of what we would call the &quot;Scientific Method.&quot; People analyzed, examined, questioned and improved these things over time. There is a ton of scientific rationalism in Creation.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why Essence can never be examined, analyzed or judged when everything else in the setting can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:02:55-08:00","id":367751,"title":"","content":"I think that the root cause of a lot of these problems is the conceit in earlier books that &quot;mote expenditure causes errors in the Loom.&quot; Seriously, that was just not a good idea at all. Even beyond the whole question of &quot;How many motes does it take to break reality?&quot; the deeper issue is that the gods who are supposed to be managing shit have to spend motes to do that management. A good of rain and storms doesn't have any innate ability to adjust rain and storms independent of his charms, and those are going to cost motes. The implication that managing reality actively breaks it in other parts is just silly. <br /> <br /> Even if you say that this is only true of Exalts and not of gods... Well, okay. WHY? &quot;Because something amazing happaned&quot; is insufficient explanation for me. I'd rather just do away with mote expenditure causing errors entirely. That way I can say &quot;Essence 'spending' is an act of supernal will and a minor miracle occurs, just like when you pray to the God of Bountiful Harvests and get one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/680-adarael","name":"Adarael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:16:25-08:00","id":367768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367684#post367684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, Thaumaturgy, Sorcery and Charms and &quot;magic&quot; in Creation are all products of what we would call the &quot;Scientific Method.&quot; People analyzed, examined, questioned and improved these things over time. There is a ton of scientific rationalism in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the dude who wrote sorcery, and some Charms and thaumaturgy, I feel pretty safe saying that's not an apt descriptor. Lots of past material has suggested that it <i>is</i>, but I don't think I'm alone in disliking that (see: the removal of the term &quot;motonic physics&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand why Essence can never be examined, analyzed or judged when everything else in the setting can be. </div> </div> </div>It can be! It totally can be. It's just that empirical inquiry isn't a very useful or productive way to experience it. That's why All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight is an Occult Charm, a description and magnification of your ability to see and experience the transcendental aspects of reality, instead of being a Lore Charm or an Awareness Charm. <br /> <br /> I get that this is a hard sell, especially since I think at least the vast majority of this forum subscribes pretty whole-heartedly to scientific rationalism, or something like it. I mean, I come from a faith that has a long tradition of interrogating and questioning the divine and am an atheist on top of that, so I get the resistance to &quot;Essence is mysterious and ineffable.&quot; But Creation is a world in which spirituality and spiritual experience are major, indispensable elements of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:21:15-08:00","id":367772,"title":"","content":"The real problem with developer/author claims that one can't apply the scientific method to Essence (and the given example about it) are thus:<br /> <br /> 1) You're taking the player-base from a setting where it was explicitly true that it COULD be measured to a setting where it's explicitly true that it CANNOT, claiming it's the &quot;same world&quot; so to speak, and then not explaining in any terms how this is actually better, as opposed to simply different. Rather, what you might term as better is seen as something of an authorial conceit. This can be summed up in the statement &quot;It clashes with what we know about the setting&quot;. Sorcery (as players currently understand it) requires research and trial-and-error testing. Wherever results are repeatable enough to produce trial and error, the scientific method can be applied.<br /> <br /> 2) Wherever a two discreet uses of an effect produce the same result using the same fuel, so to speak, the scientific method applies. Saying that a character cannot determine that two characters using &quot;Glorious Solar Attack Alpha&quot; use the same amount of mystical prowess to achieve the same results is an insult to the idea of the intelligent character. Again, this relies on the player bases current understanding of charms. It may well be the current development paradigm that no two uses of a charm can be identical, or that no two characters can have identical expressions of the same charm. If that's the case, though, that should be a sidebar. This can be summed up as &quot;Two characters both pay three motes for effect A. How does someone who can see mystical energy not notice this?&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) In reference to understanding particles and love, the author example only holds water if the character doing the math has no method to manipulate said particles. This actually strikes me as literally a perfect example of how Three-Fold Binding of the Heart might have been invented. Since it, as last printed, literally forced people to fall in love with you. There was also a Sidereal charm that was pretty infamous for destroying love. Of course, that one was VERY mystical, and involved removing someone's name from a list. But that's cause and effect. SO you CAN apply the scientific method to it. It just very well may be that your scientific answer is &quot;This list controls the potential to be loved. Things not on this list cannot be loved.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I am totally down with the answer that even if you COULD somehow detect these things, the technology, hell, even the foundational principles for said technology, might not exist. It might even be that the mathematics to quantify it outside of certain very specific scenarios and methods, such as Sorcerous Workings, might not exist. I think what's REALLY going on here is a misunderstanding of what the scientific method IS. I expect that rational observation of phenomena in Creation leads one to mystical and transcendent answers. When you apply the scientific method in Creation, you cannot get answers that are useful to people who do not exist in certain transcendent states. I also expect it tends to break down around the works of the Exalted and the more powerful gods. Just because I honestly don't believe most higher mathematics properly describe the functions of creation.<br /> <br /> Rational observation that produces repeatable results is impossible to avoid in the context of a game system. Impossible. That's sort of how systems work. Okay it's exactly how systems work. BUT it doesn't mean those observations always provide data that can explain things. Exaltation being a miracle is cool. Exigence being a thing makes it an observable and variable phenomena. This means that a lot of miracles in the setting are phrased in ways that imply one can, with the proper senses, observe them, codify the differences, note the similarities, and basically explain how it all seems to occur. Know how something happens and why it happens are different, though. I think that's the hang up here.<br /> <br /> So lets just put this on the table bluntly. The Scientific Method won't provide useful answers because the authors are going to go out of their way to do their best to make sure it doesn't. Take that as you like it, but understand their rational in doing so. It IS a somewhat sensible claim.<br /> <br /> Authors, Devs, etc: Rationalism and the Scientific Method not existing as workable concepts is probably hard for most people to wrap their head around. It might be better to work from the angle &quot;These things are different&quot;. Rationalism in any setting where miracles and gods are demonstrable is going to include those things. It's only rational to pray to a river god for his good will when he keeps drowning your kids if you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/564-deathevn","name":"Deathevn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:24:37-08:00","id":367773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367768#post367768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that this is a hard sell, especially since I think at least the vast majority of this forum subscribes pretty whole-heartedly to scientific rationalism, or something like it. I mean, I come from a faith that has a long tradition of interrogating and questioning the divine and am an atheist on top of that, so I get the resistance to &quot;Essence is mysterious and ineffable.&quot; But Creation is a world in which spirituality and spiritual experience are major, indispensable elements of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another part of it, at least from what I've seen, is that some folks just don't really know HOW to examine, analyze, or judge things in a way that isn't done in the manner of scientific rationalism. Growing up relying on empiricism leaves non-empirical study of things partially outside their frame of reference, and that frustrates them because it makes them feel less able to engage with the setting.<br /> <br /> It's far from a universal issue, of course, but it is a thing I've encountered before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:25:19-08:00","id":367775,"title":"","content":"There are charms and sorcery that function off the idea that an effect can sense someone's intent without the user of the charm or spell themselves being aware of it. This is something that would generally require either a second aware mind or a ludicrously complex machine in our own world.<br /> <br /> So, my compromise candidate: The scientific method works to study essence, but the results are less like physics and more like sociology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:26:15-08:00","id":367776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367768#post367768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the dude who wrote sorcery, and some Charms and thaumaturgy, I feel pretty safe saying that's not an apt descriptor. Lots of past material has suggested that it <i>is</i>, but I don't think I'm alone in disliking that (see: the removal of the term &quot;motonic physics&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> It can be! It totally can be. It's just that empirical inquiry isn't a very useful or productive way to experience it. That's why All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight is an Occult Charm, a description and magnification of your ability to see and experience the transcendental aspects of reality, instead of being a Lore Charm or an Awareness Charm.<br /> <br /> I get that this is a hard sell, especially since I think at least the vast majority of this forum subscribes pretty whole-heartedly to scientific rationalism, or something like it. I mean, I come from a faith that has a long tradition of interrogating and questioning the divine and am an atheist on top of that, so I get the resistance to &quot;Essence is mysterious and ineffable.&quot; But Creation is a world in which spirituality and spiritual experience are major, indispensable elements of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be reasonable to say that Essence can be examined and studied in other ways than the scientific method? Spiritual meditations on cosmic truths? Sorcerous divinations? Consulting with the Shinma? (assuming that it's coming back in 3E)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:29:34-08:00","id":367780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367684#post367684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why Essence can never be examined, analyzed or judged when everything else in the setting can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so I'm clear, what specific parts of Essence do you want to be examined? I can see Twilight Sally studying dragon lines and trying to see how Lunar essence can be better harnessed by a manse, but when it comes to system abstractions like mote counts I don't see how it makes sense for her to Scientific Method her way to realizing that, for instance, she gains 5 motes of Essence every round she spends in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:32:59-08:00","id":367783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367776#post367776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be reasonable to say that Essence can be examined and studied in other ways than the scientific method? Spiritual meditations on cosmic truths? Sorcerous divinations? Consulting with the Shinma? (assuming that it's coming back in 3E)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of things that people in the real world do to have spiritual experiences and try to understand them. Meditation. Prayer. Contemplation of koans, sutras, or catechisms. Taking psychedelic mushrooms. I imagine that all those methods and more exist in Creation, and that at least some of them work. &quot;Meditating to increase your Essence&quot; is basically going to get you going in the right line of inquiry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:35:03-08:00","id":367786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367438#post367438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say that kinda stuff about NASA too. &amp;quot;All well and good that you there are learning all this stuff, but what is the practical value of it all? Flying to the moon ain't gonna help put food on my table! Stop wasting money on it.&amp;quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I always grind my teeth when people say that. The resources in outer space are incalculable, He-3 is likely abundant, and then there is the 24/7 solar energy we already know how to send back to earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:09:50-08:00","id":367829,"title":"","content":"It seems to me there are obvious ways in which scientific rationalism could be productively applied to Exalted - almost certainly there exist curious people who have tried to record e.g. how often a very weak spell (which is a discrete named thing in-setting across editions, while Charms have been changing in that respect) could be cast over time or between Exalts of different development of their personal Essence. I'd be astounded if Exalts with access to the fruits of these individuals' efforts (Sidereals, people with First Age memories, occultists trained at the Heptagram) didn't understand in-setting that the prayers of a cult dedicated to an Exalt restored their Essence over the course of the day.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I am totally comfortable with the term &quot;mote&quot; being an out-of-setting term only, because a mote is not like a calorie. A calorie is the amount of energy that raises the temperature of one gram of water by one degree Celsius at one atmosphere of pressure. Motes oscillate in their energy-efficiency, and often have effects that simply cannot be compared in terms of energy. Empirical inquiry is <i>never</i> going to lead you to a systemic understanding of what a single mote is able to accomplish, because the answer to that question might variously be &quot;15 watts of work for ten seconds,&quot; &quot;true love for a year and a day,&quot; and &quot;the color blue.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:45:36-08:00","id":367851,"title":"","content":"I must say that I like the canon stance on this. Something 2E did wrong for me and My group was making the core mystic spritual things like something you Could approach like a Question in physics classic. It kinda took the mystic spritual out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","user":"light-hero","date":".  these phones man! 01-12-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:48:30-08:00","id":367852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367780#post367780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so I'm clear, what specific parts of Essence do you want to be examined? I can see Twilight Sally studying dragon lines and trying to see how Lunar essence can be better harnessed by a manse, but when it comes to system abstractions like mote counts I don't see how it makes sense for her to Scientific Method her way to realizing that, for instance, she gains 5 motes of Essence every round she spends in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, it should be possible to know that Spirit A has a bigger pool of Essence than Spirit B, and that Solar A has a bigger Essence Pool than Solar B. It should even be possible, using the correct charms, to calculate how large someone's Essence pool is, how many motes it costs to fuel a given charm, and therefore how often someone can use a charm.<br /> <br /> And let's be clear - you don't even really need the concept of motes to calculate Essence pools.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can easily imagine Sally Twilight in the First Age making an Artifact box, which you can channel Essence into.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, look. I just filled 5 of these boxes with my Essence, and I can't fill a 6th one. That must mean I have 5 boxes worth of Essence. Dawn Caste Dave over there was able to fill 7 boxes worth of Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, rather than calculating Essence pools by motes (which are an abstraction), they can calculate Essence pools by &quot;boxes&quot; (out of game, each of which house 10 motes of Essence), which are discrete things in the game. So even if Sally doesn't know she has 50 motes, and indeed the word mote doesn't exist, she <i>does</i> know she has 5 boxes of Essence, Dave has 7 boxes of Essence, and she can begin performing calculations.<br /> <br /> And if that doesn't work, imagine them making identical artifacts and seeing how many of these one person can attune to before they can't attune to anymore (as their Essence pool is now empty).<br /> <br /> I can also imagine similar scenarios where Sally Twilight teaches Dave the same charm she knows, and then the two use the charm the same number of times to calculate Essence. If the charm is a 1 mote cost charm (the smallest amount of Essence you can spend) then they can get a rough count of how many motes (or boxes or artifacts attuned) they each possess.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem like rocket science to and it does feel like the sort of thing that genius Exalted in the First Age, in their quest to understand Exaltation and their own powers might have done. &quot;Even though Sally and Dave are both using the same charm, why can Dave use that charm more than Sally can? We know Charms run off of Essence. So maybe he has more Essence? Let's find out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Adding more mysteries to the game is fine and all, but this one seems like a mystery for the sake of being a mystery at the risk of ruining my verisimilitude. I just have a lot of difficulty imagining that the Exalted of the First Age didn't engage in comprehensive and detailed examinations of Essence and were never able to come to even a basic understanding of something like an approximation of the size of their own Essence pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:51:01-08:00","id":367854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367829#post367829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, I am totally comfortable with the term &quot;mote&quot; being an out-of-setting term only, because a mote is not like a calorie. A calorie is the amount of energy that raises the temperature of one gram of water by one degree Celsius at one atmosphere of pressure. Motes oscillate in their energy-efficiency, and often have effects that simply cannot be compared in terms of energy. Empirical inquiry is <i>never</i> going to lead you to a systemic understanding of what a single mote is able to accomplish, because the answer to that question might variously be &quot;15 watts of work for ten seconds,&quot; &quot;true love for a year and a day,&quot; and &quot;the color blue.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To me this is the most important point. Rules are not reflections of the game world. They're only our way of resolving conflicts and making sure everyone is having a good time. If we insist that rules must be facts, then they can become observable facts, and pretty soon we expect that one of the long-lived super-geniuses of the setting will have reverse-engineered character sheets and a copy of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:27:45-08:00","id":367874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367768#post367768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be! It totally can be. It's just that empirical inquiry isn't a very useful or productive way to experience it. That's why All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight is an Occult Charm, a description and magnification of your ability to see and experience the transcendental aspects of reality, instead of being a Lore Charm or an Awareness Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. The majority of the Charms dealing with &quot;Essence&quot; as a thing are in Lore, though, to the point where by and large &quot;Essence&quot; as a concept is a Lore thing rather than an Occult thing, and that seems to have been intentionally carried forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367768#post367768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that this is a hard sell, especially since I think at least the vast majority of this forum subscribes pretty whole-heartedly to scientific rationalism, or something like it. I mean, I come from a faith that has a long tradition of interrogating and questioning the divine and am an atheist on top of that, so I get the resistance to &quot;Essence is mysterious and ineffable.&quot; But Creation is a world in which spirituality and spiritual experience are major, indispensable elements of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I really feel like this is at least as much the game's doing as the community's. On the whole, it's been more consistent about presenting Essence as conforming to scientific rationalism than not, it put nearly all the Essence powers in the &quot;science&quot; ability, it emphasized the technological aspects of Essence use (e.g. things like automatic lights that turn on when you spend Essence) and presented devices analogous to modern technology that run on &quot;essence&quot;, it often depicted savants as being analogous to modern scientists, and -- subtly but I think most importantly -- it framed &quot;motes&quot; as an in-setting construct and encouraged people to think about their mechanical resources in that light. Compare D&amp;D or Vampire, which typically refer to such things as &quot;points&quot; or &quot;levels&quot; even when they are broadly analogous to setting elements, to emphasize that they're mechanical abstractions. This isn't just line drift -- it reached new heights of ostentation with DotFA, but it's been that way since early 1e.<br /> <br /> <i>Edited to add:</i> I went back to the books to make sure I wasn't talking out of my ass, and there in the glossary -- 1e defines &quot;mote&quot; as &quot;a unit used by sorcerers and savants to measure Essence&quot;, while 2e defines it as &quot;The smallest divisible unit of Essence in the parlance of savants and sorcerers&quot;. And the game seems to be actively encouraging a simulationist link between motes-as-setting-construct and the resource you spend, given the number of powers that cost 1 mote but could easily be free. So...I think that's where that came from, more or less?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-12-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:36:40-08:00","id":367878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367874#post367874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I really feel like this is at least as much the game's doing as the community's. On the whole, it's been more consistent about presenting Essence as conforming to scientific rationalism than not, it put nearly all the Essence powers in the &quot;science&quot; ability, it emphasized the technological aspects of Essence use (e.g. things like automatic lights that turn on when you spend Essence) and presented devices analogous to modern technology that run on &quot;essence&quot;, it often depicted savants as being analogous to modern scientists, and -- subtly but I think most importantly -- it framed &quot;motes&quot; as an in-setting construct and encouraged people to think about their mechanical resources in that light. Compare D&amp;D or Vampire, which typically refer to such things as &quot;points&quot; or &quot;levels&quot; even when they are broadly analogous to setting elements, to emphasize that they're mechanical abstractions. This isn't just line drift -- it reached new heights of ostentation with DotFA, but it's been that way since early 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, very true. It's something we're deliberately try not to reproduce with Third Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:41:48-08:00","id":367885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367878#post367878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, very true. It's something we're deliberately try not to reproduce with Third Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can forgive you for not calling them &quot;essence points&quot;, because god damn that word gets used for a lot of things! But...yeah. Obviously, this is all in the context of the previous games for most of us still!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:54:21-08:00","id":367900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can easily imagine Sally Twilight in the First Age making an Artifact box, which you can channel Essence into.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can reinforce any argument by just contriving the existence of things that implicitly support it, and since this is a work of fiction the things it contains exist and function by design for the sake of an artistic agenda. The writers probably aren't making a setting in which a thing like &quot;Essence box&quot; makes any kind of sense. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't seem like rocket science to and it does feel like the sort of thing that genius Exalted in the First Age, in their quest to understand Exaltation and their own powers might have done.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel like Nobilis had a good way to articulate a point for a similar issue to this, in which it said that the language characters use to articulate their miracles is probably not the same straightforward language the players use. Like, the player of the Power of Extinction might state &quot;I cause all tigers to die out&quot;, while the character articulates the process with something more complex and arcane, the language that a human might use to communicate to an Estate, to preserve the idea that what is happening in character is more significant than the interface players use to control it. Among other implications I would think this would have would be the idea that, in character, different people using the same Charms actually <i>aren't</i> expending the same amount of energy, partially for recognisable, if immeasurable factors of contextual factors (like, the Melee 5 person using Hungry Tiger Technique against a mortal might not be using as much energy as the Melee 2 one fighting a Dragon Blood, even if the mechanics use the same amount of motes, and also when things like the ambient temperature of each are different), and partially for more vague, abstract, spiritual qualities (that we describe out of character with things like stunts and favoured Abilities). Mostly though, even if you did have something like an Essence box, I would say that the functions and observations in character would model the results in a manner that would view the thing in a different manner from a discrete Essence pool, and that would not be able to tell everything about the quality of a person that mechanics describe with an Essence pool. It's about the same as how in the World of Darkness, characters would not look upon a person and how certain actions seem to boost their emotional and physical energy and conclude the existence of Virtues and Willpower dots. Or how neither game has the actual probabilities of any given action align with the probabilities of dice pools. These are things that, if we want to imagine those worlds as being anything like our own, should be more complex to the people observing and experiencing them than they are with the game systems to represent them for the sake of entertainment. Personally, I would have it that the way physical and chemical processes work in Creation, and how Essence means that there is an interplay between the symbolic and spiritual and literal and concrete, that a developed scientist will look more like a Medieval or Renaissance Hermetic than a modern empiricist, where all of that theistic and mystical language is more than an interestingly aligned but ultimately unnecessary prop. Or like in Thor 2 where their observations of quantum mechanics are heavily ensconced in the concept of the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:54:58-08:00","id":367901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367852#post367852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally speaking, it should be possible to know that Spirit A has a bigger pool of Essence than Spirit B, and that Solar A has a bigger Essence Pool than Solar B. It should even be possible, using the correct charms, to calculate how large someone's Essence pool is, how many motes it costs to fuel a given charm, and therefore how often someone can use a charm.<br /> <br /> And let's be clear - you don't even really need the concept of motes to calculate Essence pools.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can easily imagine Sally Twilight in the First Age making an Artifact box, which you can channel Essence into.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, look. I just filled 5 of these boxes with my Essence, and I can't fill a 6th one. That must mean I have 5 boxes worth of Essence. Dawn Caste Dave over there was able to fill 7 boxes worth of Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, rather than calculating Essence pools by motes (which are an abstraction), they can calculate Essence pools by &quot;boxes&quot; (out of game, each of which house 10 motes of Essence), which are discrete things in the game. So even if Sally doesn't know she has 50 motes, and indeed the word mote doesn't exist, she <i>does</i> know she has 5 boxes of Essence, Dave has 7 boxes of Essence, and she can begin performing calculations.<br /> <br /> And if that doesn't work, imagine them making identical artifacts and seeing how many of these one person can attune to before they can't attune to anymore (as their Essence pool is now empty).<br /> <br /> I can also imagine similar scenarios where Sally Twilight teaches Dave the same charm she knows, and then the two use the charm the same number of times to calculate Essence. If the charm is a 1 mote cost charm (the smallest amount of Essence you can spend) then they can get a rough count of how many motes (or boxes or artifacts attuned) they each possess.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem like rocket science to and it does feel like the sort of thing that genius Exalted in the First Age, in their quest to understand Exaltation and their own powers might have done. &quot;Even though Sally and Dave are both using the same charm, why can Dave use that charm more than Sally can? We know Charms run off of Essence. So maybe he has more Essence? Let's find out.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is a natural direction to take things, and one I've seen in a lot of discussions of tabletop settings. But I think there's an important question to be asked, first:<br /> <br /> In your opinion, do the game mechanics of the mote pool translate 1:1 into the setting?<br /> <br /> Like, what really snapped this into focus for me was this example earlier in the thread:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367603#post367603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you can sit there and watch Joe Solar lift 30 tons exactly 7 times an hour</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, the thing is, folks who do weight training have a certain number of reps they can do of this or that exercise, and a certain amount of time they have to wait before doing it again. But those aren't actually integers, nor are they actually natural law, or even 100% consistent; they're emergent properties of the way the body is put together, which manifest differently per person, per day, per specific situation. Some folks are better at push-ups than sit-ups, or vice versa. Or better at bursts of activity vs endurance training. Or maybe they can do 100 reps on a bad day but 140 on a good one.<br /> <br /> Even if you were to write a tabletop RPG where feats of strength are an important part of the expected challenges a character would face, this is all, all too fine of detail to include in the system if you want it to be playable. You'd probably just have a bar, that fills based on rest and recuperation, and empties on exertion, and if you get all the way to the bottom you get tired and have to stop.<br /> <br /> And yet, when we talk about mote pools I see a bunch of people assuming that no, it's not a metaphysical version of &quot;getting tired and having to stop&quot;, these really <i>are</i> integers, they really <i>are</i> exactly the same from person to person and replenish at set rates and so forth. And I don't really see why.<br /> <br /> I mean, admittedly, yes, even if motes are a game abstraction, you can and <i>will</i> still get people IC trying to measure their relative strength, testing it out, and so forth. But I think they'd bump into the same kinds of subtleties as you find IRL with trying to quantify people's spending and recovering of physical, mental, or emotional energy in their everyday life, even given everything we know about how the human body works. These are emergent traits and don't operate on a level that you will ever find an IC measurement that maps to the ratio between Alice's mote pool and Betty's, because that ratio is a game abstraction that, in order to make the game playable, masks elements that are below the resolution of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\">To the extent possible under law, I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this post.</a>","edited":{"userid":666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","user":"Eco-Mono","date":". 01-12-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","name":"Eco-Mono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar666_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:13:38-08:00","id":367944,"title":"","content":"For that earlier question of &quot;how many joules is Essence worth&quot;, I feel as though the most accurate answer would be that characters in Creation could easily devise a unit to fit into an equation to model how much work a body (as in the physics term) is doing, and they <i>would</i> use that to describe the output of everyone from a baby to an Exalt, and would not actually equate that to the idea that there's a pool of Essence inside of you which is being used up in the course of doing that work. I mean, if you want to calculate the energy it would take to use a Melee Charm to cut through an oak door, that makes sense, but characters would not view the difference between the Charm-enhanced attack and a regular one that would fail to cleave the door as the energy value of the mote cost of the Charm, they'd view it as the difference between trying hard enough and not doing so. Being Exalted is <i>why</i> you're capable of mustering up this greater degree of energy, but it probably amounts to about the same as why one could, say, perform better when in a personally meaningful and relatively low stress situation; those thing don't have an empirical value, they're just a context in which you can get the most out of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:36:46-08:00","id":367978,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the vagaries of dice and the existence of perfect effects tend to skew any equations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:58:20-08:00","id":367990,"title":"","content":"Only a very poor scientist does only a single trial of an experiment. Over a sufficiently large number of trials the results of the dice average out. This is why every good experiment runs a lot of trials, specifically to eliminate random chance through averages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:59:36-08:00","id":367991,"title":"","content":"Hmm, now I'm thinking of John's notion of magic as a kind of reversal of entropy, and wondering... if, based on its structure one calculated the work that would be necessary to cut through a stone pillar in a single stroke, and calculated the biochemical energy (and transition to kinetic energy) that a human body would require to do that work, and then observed and measured an Exalt cutting through that pillar where the work necessary to do so was obviously expended, but the human body had &quot;used up&quot; only the energy required to cut something much easier, would they view it as an unobserved factor that has to logically account for the extra energy, or an instance in which the input to a process resulted in a greater output?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:00:16-08:00","id":367992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367990#post367990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a very poor scientist does only a single trial of an experiment. Over a sufficiently large number of trials the results of the dice average out. This is why every good experiment runs a lot of trials, specifically to eliminate random chance through averages.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the problem of having all these people with their charms of differing efficiency to do that many trials. Also perfects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:26:41-08:00","id":368024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367991#post367991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, now I'm thinking of John's notion of magic as a kind of reversal of entropy, and wondering... if, based on its structure one calculated the work that would be necessary to cut through a stone pillar in a single stroke, and calculated the biochemical energy (and transition to kinetic energy) that a human body would require to do that work, and then observed and measured an Exalt cutting through that pillar where the work necessary to do so was obviously expended, but the human body had &quot;used up&quot; only the energy required to cut something much easier, would they view it as an unobserved factor that has to logically account for the extra energy, or an instance in which the input to a process resulted in a greater output?</div> </div> </div> </div>The tendency is to go for an unobserved factor assuming the other equations are reasonably well understood, as you seem to be implying. It's how the dark matter and dark energy became a thing. Not enough observable matter in galaxies to hold them together. Not enough energy in the universe to account for its rate of expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:54:26-08:00","id":368056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367944#post367944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that earlier question of &quot;how many joules is Essence worth&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How many joules is Dace's Daceness worth?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:05:37-08:00","id":368063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368056#post368056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many joules is Dace's Daceness worth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Set him on fire and stick him in a Calorimeter. We'll find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:24:02-08:00","id":368073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368063#post368063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set him on fire and stick him in a Calorimeter. We'll find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You can't really tell if part of what burned was superfluous in making Dace who he is. For instance, Dace weighting 1 Kg less or more would give different results, but would a small difference in weight change his essential Daceness? Could possibly be argued either way. If he has Evocations for his golden spatula in Ex3, should it be burned alongside him? His connection to the artifact could be considered part of who he is, after all. How many calories is a given moral code? An opinion about a particular piece of poetry recited to him by Risa?<br /> <br /> Then there is the certain thing your calculations won't include: both of his souls and his Exaltation will not be burned away and turned into calories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:32:53-08:00","id":368087,"title":"","content":"Well if we're going to thorough, may as well use a matter-anti-matter reaction.<br /> <br /> The chemistry of a soul is a little bit of an unknown, but I'm sure we could find a balance in the Underworld and mass his Hun and Po. Then use good ole E=Mc<sup>2 </sup>to find the energy of a soul.<br /> <br /> Actually, probably could have started with the Math for a rough estimate. A precise enough balance might even allow us to find the Mass-Energy of the Essence Dace uses in his charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:43:50-08:00","id":368113,"title":"","content":"Do they teach nothing in schools now a days? Obviously you use the Green Fire of Malfeas, which is known to burn things like souls and moral codes away, instead of any mundane flame. Note your calorimeter must be made of the magical materials and you must correct for lingering hate and madness from the fire itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:54:02-08:00","id":368129,"title":"","content":"Hate should be pretty easy, we have chemical formulas for that I'm pretty sure given a burn time and area burned we can probably subtract that out. Madness is something else entirely, it's pretty non-specific in that it covers a great many things.<br /> <br /> I think we will probably have to settle for a battery of experiments in which we set subjects on fire with Green Fire, get some numbers and work out the mass-energy of hate and madness over a given burn time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:48:23-08:00","id":368189,"title":"","content":"Somehow I imagine that if an Exalted savant actually came up with a formula for hate, there would be a bunch of people to say &quot;no, <i>that's</i> not hate, it doesn't cover cases X Y Z.&quot; Operationalizing amorphous social concepts is a pretty tricky business, and even the metody, who are in a very broad sense &quot;hate elementals&quot;, express that concept in a complex and variable way. There's also no particular reason to assume that the set of things which constitute &quot;hate&quot; (itself an amorphous cloud that's impossible to pinpoint in a binary way) occupies a tidy space in terms of energy -- e.g. it could be that if hate has energy, it can have a hugely varied amount of energy without changing substantially <i>as hate</i>.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, of course, your ability to do these things in the game follows from the desires of the setting developers and GM, because this is miles outside the default play space in the land of totally-made-up technobabble. So there are really no assumptions about it that a player can bring to the table because it's so far afield that the laws of the universe are subservient to narrative need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T20:11:18-08:00","id":368203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2008/10/081028205658.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/images/scidaily-icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2008/10/081028205658.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> Brain&amp;apos;s &amp;apos;Hate Circuit&amp;apos; Identified </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2008/10/081028205658.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2008/10/081028205658.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> People who view pictures of someone they hate display activity in distinct areas of the brain that, together, may be thought of as a &amp;quot;hate circuit,&amp;quot; according to new research. </div> </div> </div><br /> Hate seems to be a pretty discreet thing, though I was kind of assuming there would be a chemical specifically associated with Hate that I could calculate out of the reaction.<br /> <br /> As I pointed out before, it probably wouldn't be to hard to devise a set of experiments to identify the hate and madness energies produced in a burn of given size and duration. Probably something involving twins.<br /> <br /> Though really the 10,000 years of suffering for the souls destroyed by Green Fire might make said experiments take a little to long to determine the energy of a pair of souls.<br /> <br /> Maybe that Necromancy spell that lets you pull out your Po soul could be useful in identifying the energy of a soul. The very least you could try massing your Po once you've pulled it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T20:47:09-08:00","id":368220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368063#post368063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set him on fire and stick him in a Calorimeter. We'll find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dace that can be burned is not the true Dace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T21:18:44-08:00","id":368247,"title":"","content":"This thread is strange. When informed that there is a setting where the scientific method is not a useful method of inquiry, it seems uninspired to blankly reject or contradict the premise. It's much more interesting to explore what sort of world that must be, where the most basic system of learning is not reliable. A world without the scientific method is a world without empiricism, and a world without empiricism is a world without laws. Everything is subjective, nothing can be known. Simultaneously, anything can be discovered, nothing is solipsistic. There may exist certain mathematical patterns, but none are strictly enforced. Does the earth concern you? Walk far enough from the Pole of Earth, and it will trouble you no more. What are distance and walking? Illusions made real by the feet. Meditate long and empty yourself, and it will trouble you no more. What are meditation and emptiness? Illusions made real by the mind. Just forget the earth and be forgotten. Simple enough for a charm. Or maybe not. Is Pasiap watching?<br /> <br /> Look. This is more fundamental than the lack of conservation laws, or quantifiable properties of matter. Those are the scent of the lotus, not the lotus itself. No scientific method means that experience does not inform prediction. Root, stem, and blossom, all of repeatable observation is thrown out. What remains true is: some things are, others are not. What else to call it but Essence?<br /> <br /> This is a setting where existence is personal, and visceral, and may be invested in the voices and the blades of the wise, to make them more real than the fragile things of lies and iron lesser men hold. What stores can be told in such a place? Different ones than ours, to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T21:39:07-08:00","id":368272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368247#post368247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is strange. When informed that there is a setting where the scientific method is not a useful method of inquiry, it seems uninspired to blankly reject or contradict the premise. It's much more interesting to explore what sort of world that must be, where the most basic system of learning is not reliable. A world without the scientific method is a world without empiricism, and a world without empiricism is a world without laws. Everything is subjective, nothing can be known. Simultaneously, anything can be discovered, nothing is solipsistic. There may exist certain mathematical patterns, but none are strictly enforced. Does the earth concern you? Walk far enough from the Pole of Earth, and it will trouble you no more. What are distance and walking? Illusions made real by the feet. Meditate long and empty yourself, and it will trouble you no more. What are meditation and emptiness? Illusions made real by the mind. Just forget the earth and be forgotten. Simple enough for a charm. Or maybe not. Is Pasiap watching?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't wanna say that Creation <i>doesn't have</i> empiricism. Rocks and sparrows will not defy the eye of scientific inquiry in the same way that the fundamental spiritual substance of existence does.<br /> <br /> But it's probably useful to remember that Creation's thinkers will have a much great bias for spirituality than most of us are used to!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 01-13-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:02:58-08:00","id":368278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368272#post368272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna say that Creation <i>doesn't have</i> empiricism. Rocks and sparrows will not defy the eye of scientific inquiry in the same way that the fundamental spiritual substance of existence does.<br /> <br /> But it's probably useful to remember that Creation's thinkers will have a much great bias for spirituality than most of us are used to!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the point there is that it's <i>Creation</i> that may have empiricism (or something like it). The Wyld certainly doesn't. So, the laws aren't absolute. They're just how the Primeordials set things up, and if you've got the mojo, you can defy them. If there is a natural philosophy (as suggested by the Lore ability), it's a study of the work of those who came before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:16:51-08:00","id":368287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368073#post368073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he has Evocations for his golden spatula in Ex3, should it be burned alongside him? His connection to the artifact could be considered part of who he is, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be complicated by the fact that daiklaves are unique, so you couldn't isolate the spatula's Daceness from it's spatulaness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:22:39-08:00","id":368294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368287#post368287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be complicated by the fact that daiklaves are unique, so you couldn't isolate the spatula's Daceness from it's spatulaness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, not without its brother artifact, the Spirit-Severing Cleaver. With their five remaining brothers, all seven items of the Cupboard of the Cosmos, it may be possible to <i>puree</i> Dace down into his essential Dacetiness. Such are the limits of mortal tongues, however, that the Dacetiness that can be tasted is not the true Dacetiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:30:14-08:00","id":368300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eco-Mono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367901#post367901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is a natural direction to take things, and one I've seen in a lot of discussions of tabletop settings. But I think there's an important question to be asked, first:<br /> <br /> In your opinion, do the game mechanics of the mote pool translate 1:1 into the setting?\\</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, yes, it's not simply an abstraction.<br /> <br /> Joe the Solar Sword Hunter, who goes around collecting artifact swords, even in-setting can't attune to all 1000 of the swords he owns. There is a limit to the number of artifacts someone can attune to. Each artifact requires a &quot;certain amount&quot; of Essence to be committed, and once someone has committed too much of it, they won't be able to use any charms or attune to anything else.<br /> <br /> And Dirk Dragon Blooded probably can't attune to as many artifact swords as Joe Solar can, because Joe (as a Solar) likely has a larger Essence pool, which means that, in-setting, you could calculate that Joe has a larger Essence pool than Dirk.<br /> <br /> Isator didn't like my &quot;Essence Box&quot; idea, but as I mentioned, people can still measure their Essence through artifact attunement. Imagine a type of artifact ring that, out-of-game, costs 2 motes to attune to. From an in-game perspective, you could measure someone's Essence pool by seeing how many rings they can attune to at once. After they can't attune to anymore (because they've committed all their Essence) then you can get a variable you can calculate with.<br /> <br /> Even if people, in-game, didn't talk about motes, they could talk about how many &quot;rings&quot; someone's Essence pool is, or how many &quot;Swords&quot; it is (if they're calculating Essence pool size by how many small Daiklaves they can attune to). Exalted could even use this method to realize that it costs more Essence to attune to one type of artifact than another (Joe the Solar finds he can only attune to 10 jade Daiklaves, but he can attune to 20 Orichalcum Daiklaves, whereas Dirk Dragonblooded can attune to 12 Jade Daiklaves and only 6 Orichalcum ones).<br /> <br /> I don't mind changing things to add mysteries in 3rd edition, but this just seems like an incredibly awkward thing to change. Why is it that First Age Exalted weren't capable of doing some basic experiments like the above to figure out how much Essence they're capable of outputting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:09:59-08:00","id":368317,"title":"","content":"I beg pardon for my impending self-indulgence, but while I was peeling clementines, I was thinking about this thread, and a logical extension of my earlier post made Vance's comments about spirituality fall into place for me.<br /> <br /> In my earlier post in this thread, I mentioned that trying to systematize what a mote &quot;can do&quot; is inherently doomed to failure, because that's not how motes work; I think we'd all agree that a Charm which allows you to tap your staff in a barren desert and conjure a liter of water should cost much less than a Charm which enables a user massing 100 kilograms to jump 90 trillion meters straight up, despite both these actions requiring about 9E16 joules to do &quot;fairly.&quot; Motes have a lot of applications, from the extremely concrete to the extremely abstract, and so the scientific-reductionist approach to understanding them is not very good. You can only apply reductionism up until the point where phenomena are no longer explained by lower-level behavior, after all, and if what you terminate at is <i>fundamentally complicated</i> (in a way that the lowest-level elements of our universe, it bears mentioning, are not), you're SOL.<br /> <br /> However, Essence isn't just a fancy name for energy in Creation - as Vance and Eric Minton have been hammering on in this thread, Essence is a spiritual entity <i>that admits spiritual understanding</i>. A reductionist scientist after the model of our own universe's scientific method would have to throw up their hands in trying to figure out what a certain amount of Essence would be capable of doing, or to a priori determine how much Essence would be required to obtain a desired effect, but an enlightened occultist could arrive at the correct answers through their intimate and intuitive understanding - they grok Essence flows.<br /> <br /> Now, the scientific method isn't completely borked in Creation - Creation might have a privileged &quot;down,&quot; but I see no reason why its gravity-analogue couldn't be measured, or why gifted and curious occultists could not gain a rough understanding of how much Essence Exalted at various points along their spiritual development might have (as I mentioned before, &quot;cast this known, discrete spell&quot; seems a solid unit of standardization for motepool math, and I agree with other posters that there's no way <i>someone</i> didn't think to try to figure this out). But there will be a number of points where empiricism has to give way to mysticism, because Creation simply doesn't run on the same kind of engine as reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:32:20-08:00","id":368341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368317#post368317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But there will be a number of points where empiricism has to give way to mysticism, because Creation simply doesn't run on the same kind of engine as reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. At some point it probably does. But the idea that you can't measure Essence, or Vance's statement that the scientific method doesn't apply to Essence just seems really hard to swallow.<br /> <br /> Why can't you observe Essence expenditures, come up with hypothesis (Dragon Blooded Charms tend to work this way, Solar Charms work this way, some Dragon Blooded charms are more efficient, putting up a wall here will level out the Essence flow in this region and let me create a Demense, etc), and then perform some tests and come to some conclusions?<br /> <br /> Clearly there are plenty of statements you can say are true and factual about how Essence operates and what it can do. That is, for example, the entire point of Geomancy - to predict, understand and be capable of altering the flow of Essence.<br /> <br /> So some of the things Vance has said just seems completely contrary from the way Essence has always been presented in Exalted, and it just makes no sense to me. Like how can a manse builder construct a manse to channel Essence if, what Vance said is true, the way in which Essence functions cannot be studied or predicted in any way (as the Scientific Method doesn't work on it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:41:41-08:00","id":368345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368300#post368300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, yes, it's not simply an abstraction.... Why is it that First Age Exalted weren't capable of doing some basic experiments like the above to figure out how much Essence they're capable of outputting?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the answer to the problem, so you can come up with ways to arrive at that answer. Characters in the setting aren't aware that there's a problem. They may not care to attune to x identical artifacts, since they're not interested in discovering what players know, nor are they even aware that there is such a thing as x identical artifacts. More directly, they don't experience what the rules may suggest they experience.<br /> <br /> In the actual setting there are not 5 levels of strength or smarts or good looks. People do not leap from &quot;can lift a bull&quot; to &quot;can throw a wagon&quot; (or whatever) without passing through points in between, no matter what the rules say. Solars may not think of themselves as such. Items that are abstracted into the same class, such as a particular artifact, may not strike people as being the same thing, any more than Coke and Pepsi seem the same to some people in our world. Or if those are too close, pick two 4-door sedans in the same price range or two great cats of different species or two revolvers. More directly to the point, even a repeated, thorough test offering a Solar x identical artifacts could still fail to be useful unless we assume that the Solar is aware of how many and which items he has attuned and when he is using motes for any other purpose.<br /> <br /> I'm grateful that we're moving away from those notions in Ex3. The rules have at times done us the disservice of implying that the setting can be solved and, perhaps worse, that the solutions would be the same as what we see in the rules. Obviously that's not my cup of tea, and, while I wouldn't want to stand in the way of anyone running a game in which the characters could discover some or all rules of Exalted, I'm glad the default won't be that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368317#post368317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the scientific method isn't completely borked in Creation - Creation might have a privileged &quot;down,&quot; but I see no reason why its gravity-analogue couldn't be measured, or why gifted and curious occultists could not gain a rough understanding of how much Essence Exalted at various points along their spiritual development might have (as I mentioned before, &quot;cast this known, discrete spell&quot; seems a solid unit of standardization for motepool math, and I agree with other posters that there's no way <i>someone</i> didn't think to try to figure this out). But there will be a number of points where empiricism has to give way to mysticism, because Creation simply doesn't run on the same kind of engine as reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall some good points, but I disagree that, &quot;Cast a spell x times&quot; would be a useful and interesting inquiry that would produce the results that the rules suggest. We shouldn't assume that every Solar will progress from 26 motes to 37 to 49 to 65 or whatever it will be. Those rules are for our convenience. While it is interesting to ask what other characters do when they're not &quot;on-screen&quot; with the PCs, referencing mote pool size isn't going to produce better answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":2010,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","user":"Root","date":". 01-13-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:46:56-08:00","id":368347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368341#post368341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't you observe Essence expenditures, come up with hypothesis (Dragon Blooded Charms tend to work this way, Solar Charms work this way, some Dragon Blooded charms are more efficient, putting up a wall here will level out the Essence flow in this region and let me create a Demense, etc), and then perform some tests and come to some conclusions?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a thing characters can try to do, sure. It's going to be of limited scope. It's fine that a Dawn Caste has a sort of intuitive sense of how much &quot;oomph&quot; he needs to unleash his various attacks, or for a Twilight to try and study the way Charms of a different Exalt type of creature work and build up a body of research. <br /> <br /> What you're not going to get at is the fundamental metaphysics of Essence, and Essence is about as fundamental to Creation's metaphysics as it gets. You're not going to be able to measure the mote, comprehend and describe the truth of all things that are in equations or diagrams, or reach enlightenment through science. The more and more you plunge into the esoteric and occulted parts of Essence as it shows up in the setting, the less and less useful of a tool that scientific method will be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So some of the things Vance has said just seems completely contrary from the way Essence has always been presented in Exalted, and it just makes no sense to me. Like how can a manse builder construct a manse to channel Essence if, what Vance said is true, the way in which Essence functions cannot be studied or predicted in any way (as the Scientific Method doesn't work on it). </div> </div> </div>Yep. Past editions have described Essence as a generic energy, a sort of magical particle that Twilights can research, as stuff that really lends itself well to Exalted's creeping problem of sciencifying and technologizing everything. We are make a move away from portraying it like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:52:54-08:00","id":368353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368345#post368345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know the answer to the problem, so you can come up with ways to arrive at that answer. Characters in the setting aren't aware that there's a problem. They may not care to attune to x identical artifacts, since they're not interested in discovering what players know, nor are they even aware that there is such a thing as x identical artifacts. More directly, they don't experience what the rules may suggest they experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that the Exalted were never interested in seeing how many artifacts they can attune to, and have never considered how many times they might be able to use a charm? And they never stopped to think, &quot;That's weird. Why can't I attune to any more artifacts?&quot; Or wondered why they could only use charms so many times before they couldn't do so for awhile. And they never bothered to run any tests to try and figure that out?<br /> <br /> This seems like the sort of thing that super smart people, who were interested in their own powers, and interested in pushing the boundaries of the universe itself, might have asked and tested.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why can Solar Joe attune to 5 daiklaves, but Dirk Dragonblood can only attune to 3 daiklaves?&quot;<br /> <br /> It isn't impossible to believe that the Exalted might notice something like this, be curious about it, run some tests to find out, and come to the realization that Solars generally have more Essence than Dragonblood (for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:57:26-08:00","id":368357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368347#post368347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Past editions have described Essence as a generic energy, a sort of magical particle that Twilights can research, as stuff that really lends itself well to Exalted's creeping problem of sciencifying and technologizing everything. We are make a move away from portraying it like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to thank you all for going in that direction. I <i>really </i>prefer Essence to be closer to Qi than Lux or Calories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:58:57-08:00","id":368359,"title":"","content":"...ah, I see I've found the first thing in 3E I will houserule away with extreme and virulent prejudice. I suppose something had to replace the 2E Abyssal fluff.<br /> <br /> (I guess in a way, the idea that examining the fundamentals of the universe with science and empiricism is considered &quot;a problem&quot; instead of &quot;an excellent thing&quot; is the beating heart of my worries that 3E, despite my deep and abiding excitement for the system and the large amounts of money I offered up to the Kickstarter, is Not Intended For Me. But it's not long now until I can say for sure, hopefully.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":39,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","user":"ysadrel","date":".  Wrong Edition Correction Prana 01-13-2015, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T00:14:20-08:00","id":368365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368347#post368347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Past editions have described Essence as a generic energy, a sort of magical particle that Twilights can research, as stuff that really lends itself well to Exalted's creeping problem of sciencifying and technologizing everything. We are make a move away from portraying it like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... when an Exalt wants to create a new charm, they don't actually say, &quot;I want to be able to do X,&quot; and then think about how to go about doing X, and then practice different ways of doing X until they're able to accomplish it (that is, in short, how the scientific method works)?<br /> <br /> And when a Geomancer wants to build a manse on a demense, they don't draft out a design based on research or an understanding of how Essence flows (&quot;Oh, this Demense is fire aspect, so we'll want to use X, Y and Z to channel the Essence through here...&quot;), they just... I don't know, guess their way through it?<br /> <br /> Because that seems to be what I'm getting from your statements.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can understand that when you get down to the nitty-gritty details of Essence usage, characters might not be able to understand how it works and it becomes a mystery (similar to how, even though we know a lot about how our own universe works, when we get into sub-atomic particle theory it's still pretty damn mysterious in a lot of ways).<br /> <br /> But things like predicting what the Essence in a Demense will do when you stick a manse on it, or judging how many times someone can probably use a given charm or combo before they're &quot;empty,&quot; or seeing how many times someone can attune to artifacts and using that to calculate their potential Essence, seem like fairly basic things in setting, and I don't know if I can get behind the idea that even these were grand mysteries beyond understanding even to the greatest Exalted sages of the First Age.<br /> <br /> It feels like creating mysteries at the expense of verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* And to be clear Vance, I really am trying to read what you're saying in good faith, and am trying to parse what you've been writing. This is just currently where I am in my understanding of what you're saying. So if I'm radically misconstruing your words or your position, by all means correct me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T00:27:44-08:00","id":368370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368353#post368353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that the Exalted were never interested in seeing how many artifacts they can attune to, and have never considered how many times they might be able to use a charm? And they never stopped to think, &quot;That's weird. Why can't I attune to any more artifacts?&quot; Or wondered why they could only use charms so many times before they couldn't do so for awhile. And they never bothered to run any tests to try and figure that out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that the means we the players of Exalted use to track motes are abstracted for our benefit. I can wonder how far I can run or how many ~identical peanut butter &amp; jelly sandwiches I can eat or something, but I can come up with lots of different answers at different times, and anyway I'd quickly lose interest in an answer. We as players know how important mote pools are, so maybe our characters would care how powerful or resilient or energetic they are. But they may not know that the vigorous sparring a few hours ago or the seduction attempt just then has impaired their ability to chain cast Death of Obsidian Butterflies or to focus on handily wielding yet another uniquely powerful sword. They might say, &quot;I can't do that again - I'm tired and I can't focus,&quot; but that's very different from, &quot;I'm out of motes and need to rest for exactly 3 hours or drop my committed Charms before I can cast again.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368353#post368353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why can Solar Joe attune to 5 daiklaves, but Dirk Dragonblood can only attune to 3 daiklaves?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just highlighting this because I don't think it would strike anyone as a burning question in a mythic context. Even 3 daiklaves seems like at least 1 too many to me. However, I'm not living in that world - if you've built a fighting style around swapping your 5 magic swords in the middle of combat, you're not the type to ask these kinds of questions (or post on game forums).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368353#post368353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't impossible to believe that the Exalted might notice something like this, be curious about it, run some tests to find out, and come to the realization that Solars generally have more Essence than Dragonblood (for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>That still relies on Essence as a knowable quantity, which isn't necessarily something people would wonder about. Leo the Lumberjack can do more stuff than Alan the Apothecary, but we can just take that as a fact and not wonder exactly how many calories each one can burn before he's tapped out. Or to put it another way, we can expect a lion to win a fight against a hyena, and we don't need to measure each one's energy to start coming up with answers. If two lions fight, we still could explain which won without comparing resource pools. It's only because we as players of the game know the rules and see how many dots, how many motes, which Charms, and which items characters have that we bother to pose these dilemmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T00:29:16-08:00","id":368371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368365#post368365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... when an Exalt wants to create a new charm, they don't actually say, &quot;I want to be able to do X,&quot; and then think about how to go about doing X, and then practice different ways of doing X until they're able to accomplish it (that is, in short, how the scientific method works)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are probably as many ways of mastering new Charms as their are Exalts to master them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when a Geomancer wants to build a manse on a demense, they don't draft out a design based on research or an understanding of how Essence flows (&quot;Oh, this Demense is fire aspect, so we'll want to use X, Y and Z to channel the Essence through here...&quot;), they just... I don't know guess their way through it? </div> </div> </div>Geomancers have Occult. Through the knowledge and understanding of Essence signified by that Ability, they're capable of manipulating dragon lines and geomancy. Their methods are mystical, a little unpredictable, and contain non-replicable elements. I think you could probably make a good faith argument either way for that being scientific, but that's not really the point.<br /> <br /> Essence is <i>everything</i>. Attaining complete understand of geomancy is still just one facet of an infinitely-faceted gem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But things like predicting what the Essence in a Demense will do when you stick a manse on it, or predicting how many times someone can probably use a given charm or combo before they're &quot;empty&quot; seem like fairly basic things in setting, and I don't know if I can get behind the idea that even these were grand mysteries beyond understanding even to the Exalted of the First Age.<br /> <br /> It feels like creating mysteries at the expense of verisimilitude. </div> </div> </div>We're not using &quot;not scientific&quot; to mean &quot;unpredictable in the course of game play, just to fuck with you.&quot; The perspective needed to make complex predictions about Essence is a spiritual, rather than an empirical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 01-13-2015, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T00:59:17-08:00","id":368397,"title":"","content":"At the very least, it seems to me that the Scientific Method (and empiricism) can at least be used, to <i>some </i> degree, on dealing with Essence. The question isn't, &quot;Can you use the scientific method in conjunction with Essence,&quot; (Yes/No) but rather, &quot;How <i>much</i> can you use the scientific method,&quot; and may vary from table to table.<br /> <br /> But generally speaking, it seems to me that, the sorts of things involving Essence that you can't test tend to be of the more esoteric variety - things that are more or less outside the scope of the average game.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the things you can test, getting some understanding of how much Essence it takes to attune to a daiklave, how many daiklaves you can attune to, how often you can use a charm, what will happen if you build a demense in a certain area, what will happen to the Essence if you break that wall there, whether or not one type of Exalted generally has a larger Essence pool than another Exalt, how many times someone can probably use a given charm, etc, were likely things that were tested to some degree by the Exalted of the First Age. And they would have come to various conclusions, written treatise and such about them.<br /> <br /> While things like this may be seen as mysteries in 2nd Age (where Exaltation is <i>purely</i> a spiritual matter, a gift from the Dragons, and therefore it would probably be considered fairly heretical if you were to start testing the limits of what your Exaltation could accomplish), they probably weren't as mysterious during the First Age, and the Exalted back then probably came to various understandings that may be forgotten by the Time of Troubles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:03:35-08:00","id":368398,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, I'd say there is probably a bit of scientific thinking (though probably little exact science stuff) to the interpretation of various signs of the movement of Essence as part of the work of geomancer, but it relies more on sensibility and intuition and broad principles than hard rules. Even if there are some sort of rules to it, and there probably are, it depends a lot on interpretation and an intuitively sensing and understanding of the &quot;flow of nature&quot;. I guess it could be said to be more like understanding the Tao (or maybe understanding the Tao Te Ching as a tool to comprehend nature) than understanding engineering. Not guessing, but comprehending stuff through perceptions that are not really rational.<br /> <br /> To give an example within my area of expertise, consider traditional acupuncture: there is a scientific aspect to it up to a certain point - results can be reproduced, there are etiological causes to diseases, symptoms are considered in the diagnosis (it is not just intuitively knowing what is wrong with the patient), specific points do specific things that are cataloged, various combinations are known to give particular results, today we know quite a bit about the physiological mechanisms that make it work* and so on.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, sometimes an appropriate, well directed <i>intention </i>is considered more important than a good needle-manipulation technique or a particularly precise insertion in a point**. And manipulating the needle in a clockwise or counterclockwise motion can have different effects depending on cultural background due to the change in how you perceive that motion<br /> <br /> <br /> * Of course, in the current state of Creation, they probably wouldn't know much of those mechanisms, since it is hard to study neurophysiology with bronze age technology. That said, Exalted's equivalent of the Yin-Yang and 5-Element theories are probably much better models of that reality than they are here in our universe, so that is likely to be much less important.<br /> <br /> ** The points are really regions, so the treatment can still work when you don't get it dead center on the perfect spot. Of course, excellent technique, precision and intention following an excellent diagnosis is the ideal.<br /> <br /> Edit: Of course, any decent geomancer must also be a capable architect, but his more intuitive understanding of essence informs his more hard-science construction of a manse. He must use science to know how to support that large crystal using vines or whatever, but the reason that has to be done is not entirely rational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 01-13-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:06:11-08:00","id":368403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368397#post368397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, it seems to me that the Scientific Method (and empiricism) can at least be used, to <i>some </i> degree, on dealing with Essence. The question isn't, &quot;Can you use the scientific method in conjunction with Essence,&quot; (Yes/No) but rather, &quot;How <i>much</i> can you use the scientific method,&quot; and may vary from table to table.<br /> <br /> But generally speaking, it seems to me that, the sorts of things involving Essence that you can't test tend to be of the more esoteric variety - things that are more or less outside the scope of the average game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> were likely things that were tested to some degree by the Exalted of the First Age. And they would have come to various conclusions, written treatise and such about them. </div> </div> </div>The edge cases where &quot;system\u2260simulation&quot; gives weird results is not what we want to spotlight. Again, we're moving away from the &quot;motonic physics&quot; angle, so if you're reading a First Age treatise on Essence it's going to be more like a sutra than a set of equations. Things like &quot;let's measure Essence capacity in daiklave attunements&quot; is basically too far in the direction that eventually leads to quantifying health level and experience points, empirically discerning your own character sheet, and developing Charms to let you attack and overthrow the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:16:03-08:00","id":368410,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is a much more enlightening thread than it seemed it would be.<br /> <br /> It sounds like a difference from 1e &amp; 2e which were more loose about whether essence could be treated like ether, in a way that dispenses with spiritual aspects to leave an all pervading energy, or the lifestream, a source of energy with a spiritual dimension, a dimension which can be neglected, wastefully.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the different perspective comes from John Morke, IIRC, actually practicing martial arts and being interested in &quot;internal&quot; martial arts where GCG maybe wasn't (not sure about this) and so having more of a motive to portray that experience of keeping the process of attaining internal spiritual enlightenment from either being circumvented or just plain absent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368365#post368365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... when an Exalt wants to create a new charm, they don't actually say, &quot;I want to be able to do X,&quot; and then think about how to go about doing X, and then practice different ways of doing X until they're able to accomplish it (that is, in short, how the scientific method works)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess they'd be practicing the scientific method as much as a martial artist who practices different techniques to find what works, or a person who practices meditation to find the technique which works best for them, or a maybe even a priest who tries out different sermons to find out which one feels right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:16:55-08:00","id":368411,"title":"","content":"I sort of get what you're saying with regards to Creation, but what is this going to do to Autochthonia? Essence batteries and circuits and crap are that setting's bread and butter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:19:42-08:00","id":368414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368353#post368353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying that the Exalted were never interested in seeing how many artifacts they can attune to, and have never considered how many times they might be able to use a charm? And they never stopped to think, &quot;That's weird. Why can't I attune to any more artifacts?&quot; Or wondered why they could only use charms so many times before they couldn't do so for awhile. And they never bothered to run any tests to try and figure that out?<br /> <br /> This seems like the sort of thing that super smart people, who were interested in their own powers, and interested in pushing the boundaries of the universe itself, might have asked and tested.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why can Solar Joe attune to 5 daiklaves, but Dirk Dragonblood can only attune to 3 daiklaves?&quot;<br /> <br /> It isn't impossible to believe that the Exalted might notice something like this, be curious about it, run some tests to find out, and come to the realization that Solars generally have more Essence than Dragonblood (for example).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Knowing that Solars have more mystical power than Dragonblooded is not exactly hard. Measuring it in &quot;daiklaives attuned&quot; runs into the snag that (AIUI in 3e) not all Dailklaives are the same: it's quite reasonable some might have different attunement costs.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that attuning to multiple daiklaives is... kinda stupid as a measuring stick. What if the underlying magi-physics of it take other factors you're not accounting for into consideration?<br /> <br /> <br /> And using a Charm is, as we've noted, not a huge difference (internally) from not using a Charm. Attempts to measure how many Charms you can use before fatigue (assuming you pick something showy) run into you not realizing you used a Charm to flirt with the cute guy measuring your power expenditures. Or from you sometimes spending the extra 2 motes for greater effect without really consciously thinking about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, of course, two characters may achieve the same effect using different techniques; if the other guy only has to spend 2 motes to do what you spend 3, it might look like they are better (even on a strict rules = physics level). Let alone all other possible abstracted-away variables.<br /> <br /> <br /> They undoubtedly pushed their limits, but because the rules aren't the IC laws of physics (and Essence use is actually full of quirks and exceptions), what they discovered was not the actual game rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In much the same way that someone measuring Fireball radii IC in D&amp;D will find that not all Fireballs are the exact same size, even though the mechanics say they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:20:43-08:00","id":368415,"title":"","content":"Okay. Sounds like a fairly reasonable compromise Vance. It just really threw me for a loop when you suggested that the scientific method couldn't be used at all when it came to dealing with Essence.<br /> <br /> Now I do have a question about Occult vs Lore. It seems to me that you are treating Occult as, &quot;magical things you can't really understand,&quot; whereas Lore is &quot;non-magical things you can really understand.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is that correct? Or was I reading into it too much? If it is correct, I'm a little fuzzy on what this actually means and how it will work.<br /> <br /> To compare to the Classic World of Darkness, Lore was like Academics, whereas Occult was like Science. Occult, like Science, represented your knowledge of <i>how</i> the universe works (hard science if you will, in cWoD things like chemistry or physics). Lore, like Academics, tended to focus on things like history, societies, or economics (the so-called soft sciences).<br /> <br /> Creation is based off of (what we would term) magical principles. But, even if they are rooted in magic, Creation still has rules, and Occult is what you use to understand those rules (how spirits work, what is a demon vs an elemental, how Essence flows, what a ghost is formed out of, how you can deal with the Wyld, etc). There might be quirks and unusual things, but generally speaking, the South is hot because Fire Essence is hot and fire Essence usually burns thing, and the North is cold because Air Essence is cold and Air Essence usually freezes things, and Earth Essence tends to be very stable and nullifies the Wyld, and knowing all that would be a (fairly easy) Occult roll.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition, will Occult still be the &quot;science&quot; skill of Creation, the one that lets you understand how Creation works, and help you come to conclusions about why it does that, or will that no longer be the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:57:24-08:00","id":368427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368415#post368415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I do have a question about Occult vs Lore. It seems to me that you are treating Occult as, &quot;magical things you can't really understand,&quot; whereas Lore is &quot;non-magical things you can really understand.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore is &quot;Academic Knowledge.&quot; Occult is &quot;Magic Things.&quot; Comprehension and redirection of Essence itself is seen in Solar Lore Charms, although perception of it is Occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 3rd edition, will Occult still be the &quot;science&quot; skill of Creation, the one that lets you understand how Creation works, and help you come to conclusions about why it does that, or will that no longer be the case? </div> </div> </div>Most of the time, it'll be Lore that you're using to work out the basic facts of what's going on with stuff. Only somewhere like the Wyld, Yu-Shan, or a spooky haunted manse would Occult be the appropriate Ability for seeking-understanding-of-things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T02:30:48-08:00","id":368455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368427#post368427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the time, it'll be Lore that you're using to work out the basic facts of what's going on with stuff. Only somewhere like the Wyld, Yu-Shan, or a spooky haunted manse would Occult be the appropriate Ability for seeking-understanding-of-things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is confusing me a bit.<br /> <br /> So in 3rd edition, Occult applies to knowledge about worlds <i>other than</i> Creation?<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to know say, basic information about how Elementals function or knowledge of Elemental Courts that would be a Lore roll, since since they're a natural part of Creation. Knowledge of most Terrestrial spirits would also fall under Lore rather than Occult, if those spirits are native to Creation.?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile if you wanted to know about Fairfolk, Celestial Spirits, Demons or Ghosts, you would be rolling Occult, since they're not native to Creation?<br /> <br /> Is my understanding correct?<br /> <br /> I'm also not really grokking what you mean by &quot;Academic Knowledge&quot; and &quot;Magic Things.&quot; Creation was always presented as a setting that is inherently magical with no real divide between &quot;magic&quot; and &quot;non-magic&quot; that you might see in other settings. Occult was the equivalent to Science is the Old World of Darkness, as magic was as natural to Creation as say, physics or chemistry in our own world.<br /> <br /> If there is now a meaningful distinction between whether things in the setting are &quot;magical&quot; or &quot;normal&quot; I might have some trouble wrapping my head around the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T03:16:17-08:00","id":368493,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say: while I think AnubisXy's point about the lack of differentiation between magic and non-magic in Exalted makes sense, I wholeheartedly support Lore as &quot;academic knowledge&quot; and occult as &quot;magic stuff&quot;. I don't need the character creation rules, the 25 abilities, to represent fundamental truths of Creation, I need to them to allow me to build a genre-appropriate character. And a scholar who knows a lot about history, geography and mathematics, but isn't an expert on ghosts and demons and Raksha, and a shaman who knows about gods and demons and ghosts but can't read or write or tell you anything about the geopolitical ramifications of the collapse of the region's empire 100 years ago, seem like genre-appropriate characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-13-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T05:59:51-08:00","id":368547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368414#post368414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that attuning to multiple daiklaives is... kinda stupid as a measuring stick. What if the underlying magi-physics of it take other factors you're not accounting for into consideration?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also more like measuring how many simultaneous stable, loving relationships you can be in, rather than how many household appliances you can run off the same battery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T06:31:12-08:00","id":368559,"title":"","content":"Would it help to stop trying to measure essence in Joules and look at it more like Chi? Something that can be understood, cultivated, manipulated, and used, but cannot be definitively measured? The very thing that people who practice Fung Shui, Kung Fu, and Acupuncture deal with all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2800-astral","name":"Astral","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T06:32:31-08:00","id":368560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368455#post368455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, this is confusing me a bit.<br /> <br /> So in 3rd edition, Occult applies to knowledge about worlds <i>other than</i> Creation?<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to know say, basic information about how Elementals function or knowledge of Elemental Courts that would be a Lore roll, since since they're a natural part of Creation. Knowledge of most Terrestrial spirits would also fall under Lore rather than Occult, if those spirits are native to Creation.?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile if you wanted to know about Fairfolk, Celestial Spirits, Demons or Ghosts, you would be rolling Occult, since they're not native to Creation?<br /> <br /> Is my understanding correct?<br /> <br /> I'm also not really grokking what you mean by &amp;quot;Academic Knowledge&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Magic Things.&amp;quot; Creation was always presented as a setting that is inherently magical with no real divide between &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;non-magic&amp;quot; that you might see in other settings. Occult was the equivalent to Science is the Old World of Darkness, as magic was as natural to Creation as say, physics or chemistry in our own world.<br /> <br /> If there is now a meaningful distinction between whether things in the setting are &amp;quot;magical&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; I might have some trouble wrapping my head around the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna echo this qquestion in hope of a clarification","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:33:21-08:00","id":368600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368455#post368455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not really grokking what you mean by &quot;Academic Knowledge&quot; and &quot;Magic Things.&quot; Creation was always presented as a setting that is inherently magical with no real divide between &quot;magic&quot; and &quot;non-magic&quot; that you might see in other settings. Occult was the equivalent to Science is the Old World of Darkness, as magic was as natural to Creation as say, physics or chemistry in our own world.<br /> <br /> If there is now a meaningful distinction between whether things in the setting are &quot;magical&quot; or &quot;normal&quot; I might have some trouble wrapping my head around the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like...history is not magic. Math is not magic or supernatural. Taxonomic classifications of animals that all look like dogs is not magical. Engineering equations are not magical. Regional folklore or genealogy is not magical. I don't think that is too controversial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368455#post368455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in 3rd edition, Occult applies to knowledge about worlds <i>other than</i> Creation?<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to know say, basic information about how Elementals function or knowledge of Elemental Courts that would be a Lore roll, since since they're a natural part of Creation. Knowledge of most Terrestrial spirits would also fall under Lore rather than Occult, if those spirits are native to Creation.?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile if you wanted to know about Fairfolk, Celestial Spirits, Demons or Ghosts, you would be rolling Occult, since they're not native to Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elementals are supernatural things, even if they're &quot;natural&quot; in Creation. Likewise, spells are supernatural things, even if Sorcery is a naturally occurring paradigm (if it is - it may not be).<br /> <br /> I would assume both of those examples would be Occult. Whereas, knowing about the Battle of the Broken Ford, when a small group of water elementals besieged a town 200 years ago and brought the walls down by making the river rise up, or knowing that in the year RY 452, the sorcerer Acharn the Molten destroyed a Varangian battalion with Death of Obsidian Butterflies for daring to pass too close to his tower - that would be Lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368559#post368559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it help to stop trying to measure essence in Joules and look at it more like Chi? Something that can be understood, cultivated, manipulated, and used, but cannot be definitively measured? The very thing that people who practice Fung Shui, Kung Fu, and Acupuncture deal with all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been explicitly stated that native Charms are very much like exertions of <i>qi. </i>The fact that you no longer pay spell costs with your own mote pool but gather ambient Essence to fuel the spell lends credence to your statement as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:17:18-08:00","id":368633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368559#post368559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it help to stop trying to measure essence in Joules and look at it more like Chi? Something that can be understood, cultivated, manipulated, and used, but cannot be definitively measured? The very thing that people who practice Fung Shui, Kung Fu, and Acupuncture deal with all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like 100x more. Essence <i>isn't</i> chi, but that's gonna be a good way of thinking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 01-13-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:19:12-08:00","id":368635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368455#post368455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, this is confusing me a bit.<br /> <br /> So in 3rd edition, Occult applies to knowledge about worlds <i>other than</i> Creation?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my phrasing was confusing. Occult is, loosely, &quot;magic stuff.&quot; The only time where you would ever use it to understand basic fundamental laws of what's going on here are when you're in a place that's fundamentally otherworldly. It still covers elementals and terrestrial gods and stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:34:50-08:00","id":368651,"title":"","content":"History and geneology aren't magic, obviously.<br /> <br /> But let's consider the weather in Creation. If there's something you might want to understand about it, would you be rolling Lore or Occult? Remember that the weather in Creation is formed through the mixture of Essences, and the directions of elementals and spirits typically according to a plan drawn up at some time in the past.<br /> <br /> So would the weather in Creation fall under &quot;magical&quot; or &quot;academic knowledge?&quot; From what Vance said, that would probably be Lore, not Occult (as he says Lore is about understanding Creation while Occult is primarily used for understanding &quot;otherworlds&quot;), but that is what I am trying to figure out here.<br /> <br /> I guess another way to put it is, with delineation of Lore and Occult, into &quot;Academics&quot; and &quot;Magic,&quot; is that delineation based off what <i>we</i> (21st century people reading the Exalted 3rd edition book) would consider Academic or Magical, or what <i>the people of Creation</i> would consider Academic or Magical?<br /> <br /> Because while there are lots of things both I, and your average person in the Scavenger Lands would both consider Academic or Magical, there are probably things I would consider Magical that he might consider Academic, or vice versa.<br /> <br /> That might not seem like a terribly important distinction. But understanding what Abilities are intended to cover and how they're supposed to function is very important in a game like Exalted where a major part of your character's growth is tied up in charm trees built around Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:42:36-08:00","id":368655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368651#post368651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess another way to put it is, with delineation of Lore and Occult, into &quot;Academics&quot; and &quot;Magic,&quot; is that delineation based off what <i>we</i> (21st century people reading the Exalted 3rd edition book) would consider Academic or Magical, or what <i>the people of Creation</i> would consider Academic or Magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Stuff we the readers know is magic,&quot; although that's obviously not the exact distinction in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:49:44-08:00","id":368672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368655#post368655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Stuff we the readers know is magic,&quot; although that's obviously not the exact distinction in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's more of an out-of-game distinction than an in-game one. So in such a case, phenomenon that might seem fairly natural and normal to someone in Creation (and could be something that they might reasonably learn in school), would nevertheless fall under Occult, because it's clearly supernatural to the reader's point of view.<br /> <br /> Okay. I think I understand that distinction then, even if it does feel a little clunky off hand.<br /> <br /> But just to make it clear then, do you feel that knowledge about the weather in Creation would fall under Lore or Occult? <br /> <br /> Anyway, this conversation has been extremely enlightening Vance! Thanks a ton for taking the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:59:36-08:00","id":368682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368672#post368672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's more of an out-of-game distinction than an in-game one. So in such a case, phenomenon that might seem fairly natural and normal to someone in Creation (and could be something that they might reasonably learn in school), would nevertheless fall under Occult, because it's clearly supernatural to the reader's point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Taru the Peasant is going to know that there's something a little eerie about the glowing, elk-headed spirit who appears every third new moon, demanding prayers from the villagers so that he will continue to make the sun shine down on their crops, despite the fact that the asshole spirit is just part of his everyday life. Even if you grow up under a wise woman who can light fires with a thaumaturgic word, you're probably going to notice that it's weird and magical even if she's done it three times every day in your life. It isn't that there's no in-game distinction, just that it requires a longer, more complex explanation, such as would be found in the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But just to make it clear then, do you feel that knowledge about the weather in Creation would fall under Lore or Occult? </div> </div> </div>Lore. Unless there's a Storm Mother nearby!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, this conversation has been extremely enlightening Vance! Thanks a ton for taking the time. </div> </div> </div>Glad to help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 01-13-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:08:03-08:00","id":368688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368682#post368682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect the guy with Lore to understand how the water cycle works</div> </div> </div> </div>... wait, Creation has a water cycle?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://iambrony.dget.cc/mlp/gif/h92688__safe_rainbow-dash_animated_artist-tomdantherock_table-flip.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is just too much for me to take in, I'm outta here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:09:45-08:00","id":368689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368688#post368688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... wait, Creation has a water cycle?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://iambrony.dget.cc/mlp/gif/h92688__safe_rainbow-dash_animated_artist-tomdantherock_table-flip.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is just too much for me to take in, I'm outta here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I mean, I don't know for sure that it does. But all that rain still has to get back up to the sky somehow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:06:55-08:00","id":368709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368559#post368559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it help to stop trying to measure essence in Joules and look at it more like Chi? Something that can be understood, cultivated, manipulated, and used, but cannot be definitively measured? The very thing that people who practice Fung Shui, Kung Fu, and Acupuncture deal with all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this is a useful framework in that the things you mention are very scientific in their outlook and presentation, and would not characterize themselves as &quot;anti-empirical&quot; or out of sync with scientific rationalism. There are lots of things that we can only measure or detect by their echoes or ripple effects, but we do not consider those things to come from a non-empirical paradigm and we understand that our failure to directly measure them does not have to do with them being outside the framework in which empiricism operates. For that matter, &quot;The Way that can be expressed is not the true Way&quot;, for all its antiintellectualist gloss, is a concept with considerable resonance to and history among scientists.<br /> <br /> <br /> Part of the problem, I think, is that there's a dichotomy between &quot;scientific empiricism&quot; and &quot;spiritualism&quot; being drawn here, but those things aren't opposite or even incompatible. There are scientific empiricists who view their work as contemptuous, mechanical mastery of nature and there are scientific empiricists who view their work as communion with transcendental cosmic mysteries, and the fact that what they're doing is scientific empiricism is largely irrelevant to the distinction. Scientific empiricism has deeper roots in classical spiritualism than it does in Enlightenment-era industrial rationalism. So a spiritual-empiricist dichotomy is something that needs to be <i>put into</i> a setting for thematic purposes, rather than something that occurs accidentally, and it seems like a weird thing to put into Exalted. Empiricism is not a thing unto itself, it's a byproduct of the fact that the universe &quot;has a way about it&quot;, so a universe where empiricism <i>is not applicable</i> at a fundamental level -- rather than one with insurmountable but comprehensible barriers to certain applications, which is what we have now -- tends to scan as a universe that lacks meaningful qualities or relationships, which feels excessive as a way to re-mystify Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that ultimately this is all about trying to avoid things that seem prosaic in the way midichlorians made the Force prosaic, but I think &quot;Essence can't be approached or understood in a scientific way&quot; is kind of an awkward, brute force way of doing it, as opposed to simply being cautious about how these things are presented in the text. If the Jedi had been legendary builders who created giant infrastructural projects powered by the Force, the Force would need to be presented something very different from the amorphous mystical power that it is. On the other hand, this wouldn't require making it safe, trivial, or fully mapped-out, either -- without midichlorians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-13-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:08:30-08:00","id":368710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368689#post368689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I mean, I don't know for sure that it does. But all that rain still has to get back up to the sky somehow!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered why the First Age didn't deplete all the easy sources of iron, copper, and other mineral resources. The First Age lasted longer than most of modern history and we've played out how many mines, quarries, and other sources of such? I've been watching Alaskan gold miners on History channel shovel a cubic yard of dirt through a wash plant for a couple of flakes of gold worth maybe ten dollars and I have to say: this is not what I imagine when I picture King Solomon's Mines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:20:14-08:00","id":368720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368710#post368710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered why the First Age didn't deplete all the easy sources of iron, copper, and other mineral resources. The First Age lasted longer than most of modern history and we've played out how many mines, quarries, and other sources of such? I've been watching Alaskan gold miners on History channel shovel a cubic yard of dirt through a wash plant for a couple of flakes of gold worth maybe ten dollars and I have to say: this is not what I imagine when I picture King Solomon's Mines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's in part because gods of metals can just create a deposit of that metal. The question is (1) why would they; (2) what penalty would they face if caught that might dissuade them.<br /> <br /> IIRC Ahlat convinced/bribed some god of jade to imbue the underground area near Bent Creek with rich jade veins and then led his followers to the play through dreams, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:24:54-08:00","id":368723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368710#post368710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always wondered why the First Age didn't deplete all the easy sources of iron, copper, and other mineral resources. The First Age lasted longer than most of modern history and we've played out how many mines, quarries, and other sources of such? I've been watching Alaskan gold miners on History channel shovel a cubic yard of dirt through a wash plant for a couple of flakes of gold worth maybe ten dollars and I have to say: this is not what I imagine when I picture King Solomon's Mines.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very likely that the mineral resources of Creation are renewable through supernatural intervention (possibly unconscious, like some kind of &quot;natural&quot; phenomenon). However, getting into the specifics of what <i>kind</i> of intervention runs the risk of people wondering why gods don't magically conjure tons of jade all the time.<br /> <br /> My Shogunate Dragon-Blooded game had the ST introduce the &quot;Renewer,&quot; a worm-like behemoth who ate mineral matter and procuded precious minerals, considered an important part of Creation's geology because it allowed the natural replenishment of gold, diamonds, jade and such.<br /> <br /> So of course my Air Aspect lured it out to the coast, put it on a boat and claimed it in the name of his family. Then he started renting it out to other families who were in need of precious minerals.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods! The world is their oyster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:36:28-08:00","id":368730,"title":"","content":"Well, to go by 2E, gods don't magically conjure tons of jade all the time because that would be doing something nice for mortals. But it's probably best just to not go into the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:43:35-08:00","id":368734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368723#post368723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very likely that the mineral resources of Creation are renewable through supernatural intervention (possibly unconscious, like some kind of &quot;natural&quot; phenomenon). However, getting into the specifics of what <i>kind</i> of intervention runs the risk of people wondering why gods don't magically conjure tons of jade all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be pretty difficult and come with a reasonably hefty downside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:51:44-08:00","id":368739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368734#post368734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be pretty difficult and come with a reasonably hefty downside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd settle for &quot;it largely happens on a slow timescale that is relevant across centuries/millenia but not for anyone's day-to-day life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T11:43:56-08:00","id":368798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368730#post368730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to go by 2E, gods don't magically conjure tons of jade all the time because that would be doing something nice for mortals. But it's probably best just to not go into the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's because that's interfering in the fates of mortals, which is illegal in heaven's eyes, and they could get smelted into Starmetal for it. As noted above, Ahlat bribed the Goddesses of Jade to do this, and they all face serious charges if it ever comes to light (he also did it both to make Harborhead richer AND to increase the likelihood of military conflict in the area). <br /> <br /> In the First Age, since Solars had the Mandate of Heaven, however, they legally could ask the gods to do that sort of thing, and the gods had no real reason to refuse, and much to gain, so that's probably as good an explanation as WST...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T11:56:11-08:00","id":368808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368798#post368798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's because that's interfering in the fates of mortals, which is illegal in heaven's eyes, and they could get smelted into Starmetal for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god please please <i>please</i> do not cite this shit as remotely worthwhile behavioral-control precedent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:06:54-08:00","id":368816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368808#post368808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god please please <i>please</i> do not cite this shit as remotely worthwhile behavioral-control precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I know it's out of canon now. But Gods being punished by being killed/buried under a mountain for eternity should still be a thing in E3, so the reason for gods to not just openly conjure goods for mortals should still be there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:12:23-08:00","id":368819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368816#post368816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Gods being punished by being killed/buried under a mountain for eternity should still be a thing in E3, so the reason for gods to not just openly conjure goods for mortals should still be there...</div> </div> </div> </div>No I'm fine with that. All I was referring to was that the whole &quot;let's trump up charges to get more starmetal&quot; thing was toxic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:14:08-08:00","id":368824,"title":"","content":"Why don't gods just magically make more minerals? Probably because the power and importance of their domain and thus their own personal power and importance are dependent on how important and in demand it is in Creation. Gold isn't nearly as valuable if it is common, and the demand, value, and importance of gold has everything to do with its rarity. If the god of gold just started mass producing it, he would likely suffer a sudden dramatic drop in personal power as gold is suddenly less important and valuable.<br /> <br /> The god of dirt is powerful because dirt is everywhere, and probably does mass produce it.<br /> <br /> Rare minerals in the First Age? Likely were just mass produced in the Wyld with things like WST. Wyld shaped minerals suddenly forgotten and disused after the usurpation would dissolve into nothing thus preserving the rarity of minerals in the 2nd Age, and provide a good reason for First Age Wonders no longer working, important components disappeared because they were Wyld Shaped int existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:24:25-08:00","id":368832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368819#post368819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I'm fine with that. All I was referring to was that the whole &quot;let's trump up charges to get more starmetal&quot; thing was toxic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now that it's not made of gods, do we know yet where it DOES come from? That is, are falling stars no longer attached to the deaths of gods either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:38:46-08:00","id":368846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368832#post368832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that it's not made of gods, do we know yet where it DOES come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Falling stars. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368832#post368832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, are falling stars no longer attached to the deaths of gods either?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was the direct precursor to the &quot;trump up charges = smelt new daiklaive&quot; problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:48:18-08:00","id":368855,"title":"","content":"So, sometimes, stars just fall, huh? I dunno, given the fact that the stars are meaningful in Exalted, I kinda liked the notion a falling star was actually significant. Which led to cool visuals like the Night of Falling Stars, when all the world knew that something was drastically wrong up in heaven, because of all the shooting stars. But I can see where linking that to getting Starmetal stuff leads Bad Places for Sidereals, esp if they're meant to have better relations with the gods this time around.<br /> <br /> Never really liked Starmetal, anyway. The name just sounds bland to me. Starsteel would have been better. Well, my headcanon is that the stars are literally *diamonds* and fallen ones are where Adamant comes from, so...[shrug]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:15:48-08:00","id":368891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368855#post368855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, given the fact that the stars are meaningful in Exalted, I kinda liked the notion a falling star was actually significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says they're not? They can still be signs of great portent without being something gameable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:18:22-08:00","id":368894,"title":"","content":"Shooting stars should signify wonder and great events about to unfold, not dread and terror that the world is about to fall apart. Starmetal should be a material of great portents, not great disasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:19:42-08:00","id":368896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368855#post368855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, sometimes, stars just fall, huh? I dunno, given the fact that the stars are meaningful in Exalted, I kinda liked the notion a falling star was actually significant. Which led to cool visuals like the Night of Falling Stars, when all the world knew that something was drastically wrong up in heaven, because of all the shooting stars. But I can see where linking that to getting Starmetal stuff leads Bad Places for Sidereals, esp if they're meant to have better relations with the gods this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even if stars aren't directly attached to specific gods, the night sky is still a reflection of/meditation upon the patterns currently active in the Loom of Fate. So a meteor shower would still means an upheaval - a big, disruptive change that wasn't present in the pattern and then came upon it all at once.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, that also means that any collusion to trigger such a situation &quot;because we're low on Starmetal&quot; is probably going to make more trouble for the Five-Score Fellowship than the Starmetal was worth.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\">To the extent possible under law, I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this post.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","name":"Eco-Mono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar666_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:35:26-08:00","id":368903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368397#post368397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, it seems to me that the Scientific Method (and empiricism) can at least be used, to <i>some </i> degree, on dealing with Essence. The question isn't, &quot;Can you use the scientific method in conjunction with Essence,&quot; (Yes/No) but rather, &quot;How <i>much</i> can you use the scientific method,&quot; and may vary from table to table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's keep in mind that Exalted the game is part of the real world, so its rules have to be expressed in ways that people can understand. That means something that is mystical and ineffable in-setting will still have to be expressed clearly and factually in the rules, at least if we're expected to make heavy use of it. But the rules are again not the setting itself - they're approximations we use to avoid fighting about whether we can use this Charm or activate that artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:04:11-08:00","id":369015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=368371#post368371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not using &quot;not scientific&quot; to mean &quot;unpredictable in the course of game play, just to fuck with you.&quot; The perspective needed to make complex predictions about Essence is a spiritual, rather than an empirical one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I've been gnawing on this for awhile. I'm kind of guy who needs for a setting to have verisimilitude, and I was trying to figure out how to fit this new concept of Essence into the framework of Exalted, without having it feel too arbitrary (mystery for the sake of mystery) at the cost of ruining my immersion.<br /> <br /> Before Creation there was the Wyld, and the Wyld is filled with Essence. But instead of looking at it as, &quot;The Wyld is chaotic and also has Essence,&quot; it would be a slight shift to, &quot;Essence is inherently chaotic, and when you have a bunch of unbound Essence, it's natural state is the Wyld.&quot; This means that the natural state of Essence is pure chaos.<br /> <br /> While the Primordials forced Essence into different states to use as building blocks for their new world (through tools like the Loom of Fate), left to its own devices, Essence naturally begins to revert back into its more chaotic state. That's why, when the Loom of Fate breaks down, there tend to be glitches, and during catastrophic Loom failure (like during the Great Contagion) large swaths of Creation collapsed back into the Wyld.<br /> <br /> This also means that it's difficult to deal with Essence, since it tends to act in unpredictable ways. As Essence is an inherently chaotic substance, you can't approach it the way you might approach other things. The best you can do is come up with vague rules that Essence obeys, but you can't expect to deal with it in a rational way, since Essence is naturally an irrational, fairly unpredictable substance.<br /> <br /> So when you do deal with Essence, you have to do so through a more intuitive, spiritual manner, similar in the way you might deal with the Wyld. While the Wyld does have rules and guidelines, they tend to be vague and can easily be twisted or changed by people's expectations, desires or through sheer force of will.<br /> <br /> Does that seem like a fairly reasonable compromise or useful reasoning for why Essence is something that you can't deal with empirically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:24:09-08:00","id":369055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=369015#post369015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I've been gnawing on this for awhile. I'm kind of guy who needs for a setting to have verisimilitude, and I was trying to figure out how to fit this new concept of Essence into the framework of Exalted, without having it feel too arbitrary (mystery for the sake of mystery) at the cost of ruining my immersion.<br /> <br /> Before Creation there was the Wyld, and the Wyld is filled with Essence. But instead of looking at it as, &quot;The Wyld is chaotic and also has Essence,&quot; it would be a slight shift to, &quot;Essence is inherently chaotic, and when you have a bunch of unbound Essence, it's natural state is the Wyld.&quot; This means that the natural state of Essence is pure chaos.<br /> <br /> While the Primordials forced Essence into different states to use as building blocks for their new world (through tools like the Loom of Fate), left to its own devices, Essence naturally begins to revert back into its more chaotic state. That's why, when the Loom of Fate breaks down, there tend to be glitches, and during catastrophic Loom failure (like during the Great Contagion) large swaths of Creation collapsed back into the Wyld.<br /> <br /> This also means that it's difficult to deal with Essence, since it tends to act in unpredictable ways. As Essence is an inherently chaotic substance, you can't approach it the way you might approach other things. The best you can do is come up with vague rules that Essence obeys, but you can't expect to deal with it in a rational way, since Essence is naturally an irrational, fairly unpredictable substance.<br /> <br /> So when you do deal with Essence, you have to do so through a more intuitive, spiritual manner, similar in the way you might deal with the Wyld. While the Wyld does have rules and guidelines, they tend to be vague and can easily be twisted or changed by people's expectations, desires or through sheer force of will.<br /> <br /> Does that seem like a fairly reasonable compromise or useful reasoning for why Essence is something that you can't deal with empirically?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget that the Wyld is <i>narrative</i> chaos, and obeys story logic. So in its natural state you need things like a sense of the dramatic and aesthetic appreciation to get a handle on how it will behave. It spawns sentient stories as a natural by product.<br /> <br /> Things with defined legends such as powerful gods and primordials impart an aspect that causes the essence to behave in a certain way according to their legend. Solar essence more naturally flows in pyramids than it does caves for example because of the symbolic resonance between being high up and pointing toward heaven and the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:29:19-08:00","id":369061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=369055#post369055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that the Wyld is <i>narrative</i> chaos, and obeys story logic. So in its natural state you need things like a sense of the dramatic and aesthetic appreciation to get a handle on how it will behave. It spawns sentient stories as a natural by product.<br /> <br /> Things with defined legends such as powerful gods and primordials impart an aspect that causes the essence to behave in a certain way according to their legend. Solar essence more naturally flows in pyramids than it does caves for example because of the symbolic resonance between being high up and pointing toward heaven and the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's kind of what I was getting at. The &quot;logic&quot; of Essence would be more of a spiritual or intuitive one, in the same way that dealing with the Wyld isn't really something you can read a book on, and then go out and do. Every time you go there, things are different, and while there are some rough guidelines, it's not really like you can really predict how something will unfold.<br /> <br /> Assuming Essence works along similar lines (and it seems in 3rd edition it will), then it just took me a slight shift in perspective to explain why that is, without breaking the verisimilitude of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:23:55-08:00","id":369189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=369061#post369061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's kind of what I was getting at. The &quot;logic&quot; of Essence would be more of a spiritual or intuitive one, in the same way that dealing with the Wyld isn't really something you can read a book on, and then go out and do. Every time you go there, things are different, and while there are some rough guidelines, it's not really like you can really predict how something will unfold.<br /> <br /> Assuming Essence works along similar lines (and it seems in 3rd edition it will), then it just took me a slight shift in perspective to explain why that is, without breaking the verisimilitude of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. A minor note though, apparent the Wyld is what happens when there is too much energy in the essence. When it gets &quot;excited&quot; as it were. The wyld zones around the Western Volcano calderas was the result of spillage from the fertility engines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:44:53-08:00","id":370024,"title":"","content":"So, if I understand this thread correctly, a savant in Creation would approach an attempt to understand the aforementioned 'water cycle' or 'weather' through a series of observations that we, in the real world, would see as the scientific method, while <i>concurrently</i> meditating on the the interplay of Essence underlying those observations based on local geomancy, the role and purview of relevant spirits, the differences between how Essence is observed in Creation versus it's 'natural' state in the Wyld (or maybe even tainted state in Shadowlands). In so doing, they would achieve an understanding of 'the water cycle' or 'weather' in the kind of spiritually intuitive way Vance seems to be suggesting, but also in a way that makes it clear that the scientific method is a tool that is usable in Creation, even if its purpose is to produce something upon which one meditates to subsequently unravel the mysteries we might call 'a law of nature'.<br /> <br /> A savant would not approach a study of Essence directly however because that can be as directly observed in Creation as it can be here (ie, it can't). What can be observed is the interplay of things, the flow of Essence. So one studies the various ways Essence plays out: the water cycle, weather, sorcery, the awe inspired by a beautiful sunset, the nature of love (or hate), why are puns annoying, etc. You make observations, test your theories, meditate upon those results, make intuitive leaps of 'logic', and begin again, furthering this scientifically spiritual understanding. And the further you proceed, the less you meditate on real phenomena, but rather the underlying spiritual underpinnings of 'why that might be'.<br /> <br /> It's less, 'a butterfly beats its wings in Lookshy and there is a hurricane in Halta', but rather 'in what way is the butterfly in Lookshy really the same thing as the hurricane in Halta?'<br /> <br /> Does that sound right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We are Ten Thousand strong.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/621-howling-coyote","name":"Howling Coyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:28:52-08:00","id":370088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howling Coyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370024#post370024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less, 'a butterfly beats its wings in Lookshy and there is a hurricane in Halta', but rather 'in what way is the butterfly in Lookshy really the same thing as the hurricane in Halta?'<br /> <br /> Does that sound right?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is a raven like a writing desk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:25:33-08:00","id":370131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howling Coyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370024#post370024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I understand this thread correctly, a savant in Creation would approach an attempt to understand the aforementioned 'water cycle' or 'weather' through a series of observations that we, in the real world, would see as the scientific method, while <i>concurrently</i> meditating on the the interplay of Essence underlying those observations based on local geomancy, the role and purview of relevant spirits, the differences between how Essence is observed in Creation versus it's 'natural' state in the Wyld (or maybe even tainted state in Shadowlands). In so doing, they would achieve an understanding of 'the water cycle' or 'weather' in the kind of spiritually intuitive way Vance seems to be suggesting, but also in a way that makes it clear that the scientific method is a tool that is usable in Creation, even if its purpose is to produce something upon which one meditates to subsequently unravel the mysteries we might call 'a law of nature'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most scholars aren't gonna get into the transcendental part of understanding Essence. If a savant wants to understand the water cycle, he'll spend time observing rain falling, evaporating, and condensing into clouds. Maybe there are some gods involved; they might give useful pointers or screw up his day. The spiritual understanding needed to understand how Essence is flowing when rain becomes rivers becomes clouds is much more difficult to access, but also not really necessary if you already know the rudiments. <br /> <br /> The questions where you gotta throw away empiricism and turn to spiritual experience are generally going to be either concerned with magic and spirituality, or with the very most fundamental precepts of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:33:15-08:00","id":370213,"title":"","content":"It's also completely normal that empiricism isn't 100% reliable. The Primordials built Creation essentially out of (and is currently floating in) Narrative... sort of. There are bound to be quirks that stem out of that, creating odd differences compared to our world - like &quot;Uniqueness&quot; being an actual Thing (where unlike in our world, something being unique is a quality that affects how the object acts within the confines of reality) -- though the Loom of Fate probably plays a part in that.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: how far does the Loom go into upholding Empiricism? Did Creation come built-in with hard physics, or were those added later? (I think this was covered in books I didn't get to read)<br /> <br /> In this perspective it makes sense that Essence isn't 100% rational: maybe it doesn't follow hard logic so much as Narrative Structure, and so different Savants, having different &quot;roles&quot; and &quot;scenes&quot;, experience it differently.<br /> <br /> This, of course, is going into hugely meta territory, but I feel like It's something that's kind of subtly been there since the beginning. Like how doing something in a cool way actually makes that thing easier to do (I know system != simulation, especially where stunts are concerned, but in this case I find it funny, and it (unintentionally?) supports this idea of &quot;Essence is narrative&quot;, so I'm sticking with it.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:27:39-08:00","id":370279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370213#post370213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is to say: how far does the Loom go into upholding Empiricism? Did Creation come built-in with hard physics, or were those added later? (I think this was covered in books I didn't get to read)</div> </div> </div> </div>Empiricism isn't really a property in and of itself. The applicability of empiricism is a byproduct of the fact that causal relationships exist, and that there's an association (if not necessarily a straight line) between inputs and outputs. You can't really get away from it, which is why antiempirical viewpoints kind of puzzle me. Even if you begin with the thesis that there is no fundamental order to the universe and every rule is sometimes broken, empiricism remains applicable, because you can use empiricism to individually rule out hypotheses that propose unbreakable rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T17:34:04-08:00","id":370406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370213#post370213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also completely normal that empiricism isn't 100% reliable. </div> </div> </div> </div>Empiricism isn't completely reliable in reality! That's Heisenberg's doleful curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T17:48:00-08:00","id":370434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370406#post370406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empiricism isn't completely reliable in reality! That's Heisenberg's doleful curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using my last fifth-level spell slot to cast Heisenberg's Doleful Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:16:22-08:00","id":370610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370279#post370279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Empiricism isn't really a property in and of itself. The applicability of empiricism is a byproduct of the fact that causal relationships exist, and that there's an association (if not necessarily a straight line) between inputs and outputs. You can't really get away from it, which is why antiempirical viewpoints kind of puzzle me. Even if you begin with the thesis that there is no fundamental order to the universe and every rule is sometimes broken, empiricism remains applicable, because you can use empiricism to individually rule out hypotheses that propose unbreakable rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. It's faster to say &quot;uphold empiricism&quot; rather than &quot;uphold the causal consistency needed to be able to consistently apply the principles of empiricism in a coherent manner&quot;. I didn't think I needed to rigorously define it for the message to come across. I was hoping to avoid <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/index.php?db=comics&amp;id=3470\" target=\"_blank\">technicality club</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:55:05-08:00","id":371039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367081#post367081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a &quot;God is not the River&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> Fate is important, and it can have an effect on people. If someone is fated to not fall in love, while it is <i>possible</i> that they will (because Fate can always be glitched and other gods/Exalted, etc can use their powers to change things), it's terribly unlikely. Likewise if someone is fated to fall in love with another person, then they probably will (barring some outside interference).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if none of that matters, and it's just &quot;descriptive&quot; rather than &quot;prescriptive&quot; then the entire Bureau of Fate is pointless, and that isn't much fun for Sidereal players. Why should Players be too worried about planning Fate and running around fixing things when they go wrong, if the only issue is that someone's paperwork ended up being a little off?<br /> <br /> Fate does matter, it has an effect on things, and when it gets messed up, it's important for Creation that things be put back on track, not just because it messed up some gods paperwork.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*<br /> <br /> I mean, when Prince Joe peeks out of his carriage and falls in love with the commoner walking across the street, that isn't really spiritual or a mystery or anything like that. To <i>him</i> it probably is, yes. But we, as readers, know it's something that was probably approved by a planning committee up in Yu-Shan several years ago, and only after they had weighed out the pro's and con's to determine if it's better for the future of Creation or not.<br /> <br /> And then, when all is said and done, maybe they had to send a Sidereal agent to make sure that the prince fell in love with that commoner and not the Fair Folk next to her that was trying to tempt him.<br /> <br /> Some of the things that other settings treat a mysterious, Exalted treats differently. And I have always found that to be something that makes Exalted kind of cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, somehow I doubt &quot;humans are just puppets acting out a script written by gods&quot; is intended, given, you know, the rather long history of the Dev's saying that the various implementations of that idea with regards to Spirits, Yozi, etc are really bad. <br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Fate doesn't really seem to work like you're describing. You're using the normal, real world definition of fate(at least in the US). In exalted, fate doesn't seem to deal as much with actually forcing someone to do a certain thing. Just look at what Sidereal astrology does: it makes certain actions more effective against someone/more effective for someone to do. It doesn't dictate that they must do things.<br /> <br /> Plus, I didn't say that fate wasn't important. I said that the paperwork wasn't actually something that controlled 99.99999999% of the population with near perfect accuracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:50:05-08:00","id":371609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=370610#post370610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware. It's faster to say &quot;uphold empiricism&quot; rather than &quot;uphold the causal consistency needed to be able to consistently apply the principles of empiricism in a coherent manner&quot;. I didn't think I needed to rigorously define it for the message to come across. I was hoping to avoid <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/index.php?db=comics&amp;id=3470\" target=\"_blank\">technicality club</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I get that. But, I mean, OK, proceeding with this reasoning: the Loom is necessary to uphold empiricism. Normally it does this more or less consistently, but sometimes it messes up, and at those times it's possible for empiricism to fail. As a Sidereal, reasoning that a failure in empiricism might reflect issues with the Loom or the presence of meddlers is using empiricism. If you make changes and then check to see if the failure in empiricism goes away, that's also using empiricism, especially if that knowledge has some applicability to similar future situations.<br /> <br /> One can't escape the applicability of empiricism by positing that the laws of nature are contingent on a higher power -- all one can do is displace it, like the &quot;endless recursion of higher-order languages&quot; solution to self-reference paradoxes. Any sort of causality or functional relationship is sufficient for empiricism to apply. What you can <i>get</i> out of empiricism will often be pretty limited, but it's difficult to imagine a situation where you could get something through methods <i>other</i> than empiricism, but not through any form of empiricism, since you could always have the other method serve as an &quot;oracle&quot; and then build an empirical framework on the oracle.<br /> <br /> This is why it's best not to go down this path. There are ways to get the same practical effect with much less absurdism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-15-2015, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:11:29-08:00","id":371776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=371609#post371609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any sort of causality or functional relationship is sufficient for empiricism to apply. What you can <i>get</i> out of empiricism will often be pretty limited, but it's difficult to imagine a situation where you could get something through methods <i>other</i> than empiricism, but not through any form of empiricism, since you could always have the other method serve as an &quot;oracle&quot; and then build an empirical framework on the oracle.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that essence manipulation is tied into states of consciousness. You can't trial and error your way into magic, as the results of your experiments are largely dependent on the subjective &quot;enlightenment&quot; you feel at the time. If magic requires some variety of religious experience to function it's much more productive to approach magic with an air of spiritualism. And while you could make a case that this still technically allows for empiricism, it makes perfect sense that Creation's guides to achieving emotional states are going to look more like sutras than psych textbooks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T09:39:18-08:00","id":372628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=371776#post371776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that essence manipulation is tied into states of consciousness. You can't trial and error your way into magic, as the results of your experiments are largely dependent on the subjective &quot;enlightenment&quot; you feel at the time. If magic requires some variety of religious experience to function it's much more productive to approach magic with an air of spiritualism. And while you could make a case that this still technically allows for empiricism, it makes perfect sense that Creation's guides to achieving emotional states are going to look more like sutras than psych textbooks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to agree with this. But it's quite different from saying that empiricism isn't applicable -- you probably used empiricism to figure out that your state of mind or cosmic awareness or whatever matters in the first place, for instance. A lot of what I'm saying is to try to emphasize that &quot;you can't determine this experimentally due to constraints or information-conservation properties&quot; is not the same as saying that empiricism is not relevant to how something operates -- there are tons of things like that in the real world, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:55:21-08:00","id":372738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=372628#post372628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree with this. But it's quite different from saying that empiricism isn't applicable</div> </div> </div> </div>That does rather tend to suggest we're looking at the wrong model of rational enquiry through. 'Motonic Physics' is reductive both as a term and an idea. It says that the basic element of Essence is math. Considering it as 'Essence Psychology' both retains the underlying approach of exploration but acnowledges the subjective, necessarily un-measurable<br /> aspects of the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T16:46:58-08:00","id":373073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine how the twilight scientists of old wept when they attained understanding of the deep structure of Essence and realized it was not a truth which their tongues could speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you meet the kilomote on the road, kill it.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:33:22-08:00","id":373115,"title":"","content":"Going back to the original premise of this thread, I feel as though there are more interesting ways to articulate massive quantities of Essence than expressing them as a kilomote (in particular terms for elaborate geomantic networks to harness them), and more interesting things to focus on in the expenditure of such Essence than effects on the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:29:07-08:00","id":373228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, you <i>can</i> reduce the soul, love, or religion to a set of physics equations. These are emergent properties of physical objects; those physical objects obey physical law; the processes which give rise to these emergent properties can be charted mathematically as a probabilistic pathway.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean you can usefully <i>understand</i> the soul, love, or religions by parsing them in this way. No matter how effective your measurements, you are using the wrong tool for the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. <span style=\"color:white\">bluh bluh</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:03:15-08:00","id":373290,"title":"","content":"The idea that knowledge of motes somehow means understanding of the way the universe works in hyperrational and hyperepistemic detail is very odd to me. It seems to stem from some mindset of reductionism that scientists and philsoophers of science have kind of been arguing about for decades now. As much as physicists like to point out everything eventually scales down to fundemental physics, how one even bothers to get there is not clear or possibly even possibly clear. <br /> <br /> This gets even weirder since in our world one can pull into question what the hell numbers even are (and that has some consquences to it) and so the results of trying to say everything can be done in math has some odd effects I don't think a lot of gamers quite get. Love, life, and purpose are not really quantifiable in quanta very well, yet in th eend it's all built from that. I just feel Essence is the same way. A mote is a thing, sure, but the way that thing goes into other things is not going to be in routes very usefully descriable of moving billiard balls in a room around, much to the chagrin of people who want to reduce all of biology to sunlight and geothermal energy moving around organic matter on the planet. It's not an inaccurate descriptor, but it's kind of useless when actually wanting to discuss biology.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:32:04-08:00","id":373549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=365885#post365885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;1000 motes&quot; is about as boring as it can get;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=373290#post373290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;..It's not an inaccurate descriptor, but it's kind of useless when actually wanting to discuss biology.<br /> <br /> And stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even though I really like the idea that you can reduce things in a world such as Creation to formula and equations, this hits the nail on the head for me. Almost every other imaginable way of conveying that information is more evocative and it adds absolutely nothing on it's own.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:44:06-08:00","id":373561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edward Eldritch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=373549#post373549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though I really like the idea that you can reduce things in a world such as Creation to formula and equations, this hits the nail on the head for me. Almost every other imaginable way of conveying that information is more evocative and it adds absolutely nothing on it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such an approach is very good at telling you <i>what</i> might happen as a result of given choices. It's very bad (outside wide-ranging assumptions) at telling you <i>why</i> you'd do a thing or which course of action is <i>best</i>. 'Why' seems like its an issue that has a strong effect on Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:45:12-08:00","id":373642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=373115#post373115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the original premise of this thread, I feel as though there are more interesting ways to articulate massive quantities of Essence than expressing them as a kilomote (in particular terms for elaborate geomantic networks to harness them), and more interesting things to focus on in the expenditure of such Essence than effects on the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metric seems wrong for Exalted anyway. You would have, like, a hogshead of Essence.<br /> <br /> This isn't as frivolous a distinction as it appears to be! Classical measurements tend to reflect the origins of counting and measurement as worldly arts, so something might involve &quot;as much essence as X&quot;, where X is, I don't know a demesne or a god or a person or whatever. Thinking of the praxis of actual Exalted, I could imagine them measuring Essence in relation to respiration.<br /> <br /> There's also been some suggestion in the past that the &quot;flavour&quot; of Essence matters, e.g. that Solar Essence is fundamentally different from Lunar Essence in ways beyond quantity, which seems appropriate and further complicates the picture.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think the big problems with this perspective come from the linkage between motes-as-game-abstraction and motes-as-setting-construct. I used to be super into the setting/mechanics linkage of Exalted, and I still like it in principle, but that sort of thing can lead to unhappy compromises. It doesn't really matter if Essence is quantized <i>somehow</i>, since lots of things are quantized even when they appear continuous to us. But presenting the quantum of Essence as being huge and relevant to the daily activities of Essence-users raises its visibility and relevance. In real life I can spend my entire life working with water, even doing chem labs, and never have to deal individually with a single molecule of water, but if I could take a cupful of water and determine that it could only be divided into 100 parts before each part became indivisible, it would make &quot;water quanta&quot; relevant in a way that they just aren't, otherwise.<br /> <br /> Motes have to be coarse-grained for mechanical reasons, and in most games if a player says they're going to reverse-engineer their power quanta by observing how many times they can use the power, you're free to remind them that it's a mechanical abstraction and that extrapolating it to things it wasn't meant to cover may not &quot;work&quot; in-game. But motes, by linking the setting and mechanics, encourage this kind of extrapolation and the consequences it implies, despite the fact that most of the considerations that go into mote pools and costs are mechanical without much thought to their setting implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-17-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T15:58:48-08:00","id":373881,"title":"","content":"Given 1st Edition Sidereals, I've always been under the impression that the Loom isn't for holding up consistency, but for upholding continuity.<br /> <br /> That is, when the Loom spins out it isn't doing so to hold up the rules of reality today, the Maidens/Spiders/Sidereal &amp; Divine Planning Committee's are cranking out tomorrow. Hence the &quot;required number of successes&quot; to allow Creation to continue being Creation. I'd always assumed that if that weaving isn't continued you'd get more Wyld instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T10:28:35-08:00","id":1525127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/365654-kilomote-and-the-loom-of-fate?p=367852#post367852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally speaking, it should be possible to know that Spirit A has a bigger pool of Essence than Spirit B, and that Solar A has a bigger Essence Pool than Solar B. It should even be possible, using the correct charms, to calculate how large someone's Essence pool is, how many motes it costs to fuel a given charm, and therefore how often someone can use a charm.<br /> <br /> And let's be clear - you don't even really need the concept of motes to calculate Essence pools.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can easily imagine Sally Twilight in the First Age making an Artifact box, which you can channel Essence into.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, look. I just filled 5 of these boxes with my Essence, and I can't fill a 6th one. That must mean I have 5 boxes worth of Essence. Dawn Caste Dave over there was able to fill 7 boxes worth of Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, rather than calculating Essence pools by motes (which are an abstraction), they can calculate Essence pools by &quot;boxes&quot; (out of game, each of which house 10 motes of Essence), which are discrete things in the game. So even if Sally doesn't know she has 50 motes, and indeed the word mote doesn't exist, she <i>does</i> know she has 5 boxes of Essence, Dave has 7 boxes of Essence, and she can begin performing calculations.<br /> <br /> And if that doesn't work, imagine them making identical artifacts and seeing how many of these one person can attune to before they can't attune to anymore (as their Essence pool is now empty).<br /> <br /> I can also imagine similar scenarios where Sally Twilight teaches Dave the same charm she knows, and then the two use the charm the same number of times to calculate Essence. If the charm is a 1 mote cost charm (the smallest amount of Essence you can spend) then they can get a rough count of how many motes (or boxes or artifacts attuned) they each possess.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem like rocket science to and it does feel like the sort of thing that genius Exalted in the First Age, in their quest to understand Exaltation and their own powers might have done. &quot;Even though Sally and Dave are both using the same charm, why can Dave use that charm more than Sally can? We know Charms run off of Essence. So maybe he has more Essence? Let's find out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Adding more mysteries to the game is fine and all, but this one seems like a mystery for the sake of being a mystery at the risk of ruining my verisimilitude. I just have a lot of difficulty imagining that the Exalted of the First Age didn't engage in comprehensive and detailed examinations of Essence and were never able to come to even a basic understanding of something like an approximation of the size of their own Essence pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know its been several years since this thread started but I've been rereading this thread, and mused on how to understand this. I think I might be able to understand this why this would not be able to work as per Vance's description. I would say that how much mote is used, in so much in that is a thing in universe, would only be able to describe part of what occurs, but not the totality.<br /> <br /> Say for example that you had two people with a Essence pool, one smaller then the other and tried to attune several Daiklaves. In your example, obiviously the person, with the larger essence pool would be able to attune more and I would say for many that would be the case. However, if for example, the person with the smaller mote pool, had a stronger metaphysical connection to the concept of swords for example, they would be to attune more, despite that in essence pools wise, this should not be possible and you can't really describe that connection in terms of motes. The equation and mathematical method doesn't account for that factor. Attunement would not be solely dependent on mote pools, you could qualitively meaure it in terms of how strong the metaphysical connection is, but not be able to quantatively describe it in a form of an equation, because how could you do that? Like say, the feelings of love cause me to use X amount of motes in one person, but in another produce an lower or higher amount of motes etc.<br /> <br /> So in summary, I would say that measuring things in terms of mote pools would be a thing and that using the Scentific Method is a thing, but only one factor out of many when using Essence, many of which can't really be measured in quantative terms. Like being affected by things such as symbolism, memories, how you were which affects the way Essence is used which you can't really measure in terms of motes or which are highly unique and idiosyncratic to the indidvual and would not have the same result with another person due to their different experiences, beliefs and even soul which would cause differing results .It would be all those things together which combine into the result.<br /> <br /> These are obviously things that are not described in the books, because they arent something we can really use OOC, but would probably affect Essence usage in universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28251,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28251-derethus","user":"Derethus","date":". 11-06-2023, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28251-derethus","name":"Derethus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}